</section>
<section id="S4.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.4.2. </span>A-session protocol.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Once <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>’s information can establish an <span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A-session</span>.
Let the <span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">task-msg</span> budgets of the <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be denoted by <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
Establishing an A-session consists of two phases: <span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">handshake</span> and <span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">transmission.</span> (see Figure <a href="#S4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 4.4.2. A-session protocol. ‣ 4.4. Agent-to-Agent Intercommunication ‣ 4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F5" class="ltx_figure" aria-describedby="acmlabel5">
