"0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{i+1},tag_{i+1}),m_{i+1}=[res_{i+1},NextTok^{RCP}_{i+1},NextTok^{ICP}_{i+1}]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 533.19 -335.43 L 564.69 -335.43 L 564.69 -343.23 L 539.05 -343.23"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 -1.0 539.05 -343.23)"><path d="M -6.06 3.74 L 0.42 0 L -6.06 -3.74 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 545.95 -327.09)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.47em;--ltx-fo-height:1.95em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="30.44" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.98)" width="103.38"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S4.F5.pic1.9" class="ltx_inline-block">
<span id="S4.F5.pic1.9.1" class="ltx_p">Verify token <math id="S4.F5.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H()</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="S4.F5.pic1.9.2" class="ltx_p">Run <math id="S4.F5.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="HMAC()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">HMAC()</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 38.13 -227.86)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10.84em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="149.94"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F5.pic1.10" class="ltx_text">Message Transmission (<math id="S4.F5.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF"><path d="M 33.24 -212.6 L 221.94 -212.6 L 221.94 -228.34 L 214.06 -236.21 L 33.24 -236.21 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 38.13 -227.86)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10.84em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="149.94"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F5.pic1.11" class="ltx_text">Message Transmission (<math id="S4.F5.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 666.43 -382.56 M 666.43 -382.56 L 666.43 -212.6 L 33.24 -212.6 L 33.24 -382.56 Z M 33.24 -212.6"></path></g></g></svg></span>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>. </span><span id="S4.F5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">A-session establishment</span><span id="acmlabel5" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">To avoid warning.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Handshake.</span>
The goal of the handshake phase is to establish an authorized, budgeted, and
cryptographically bound session between <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this phase,
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> presents the <span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span>-signed authorization token and its signed
commitment to the initiating hash chain, while <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies these values,
sets its local message and time limits, commits to its responding hash chain,
and returns the corresponding signed policy information. The agents then derive
a shared session key from their exchanged randomness, which is used to protect
subsequent <span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">task-msg</span> in the session. The details steps during the handshake are:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Initiating the A-session.</span>
Agent <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> generates a symmetric key <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and creates a personalized hash
chain of length <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{I,R}=n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{I,R}=n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> using the seed</p>
<table id="S4.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\,\mathit{addr})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖱𝖥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\,\mathit{addr})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{addr}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{addr}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for the first chain used in this A-session. The chain is:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho_{0},\quad\rho_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho_{0},\quad\rho_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H(\rho_{0},\,1,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(\rho_{0},\,1,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H(\rho_{1},\,2,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn> 2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(\rho_{1},\,2,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\vdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\vdots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho_{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho_{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H(\rho_{n^{\prime}-1},\,n^{\prime},\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(\rho_{n^{\prime}-1},\,n^{\prime},\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> also obtains the user’s signature on the root of the chain:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U}_{ICP}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{U}}(\rho_{n^{\prime}},\,Q_{I,R})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗀𝗇</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U}_{ICP}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{U}}(\rho_{n^{\prime}},\,Q_{I,R})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> then initializes two counters: <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{ICP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}][\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{ICP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}][\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]</annotation></semantics></math>,
set to <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}][\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}][\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
It decrements <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{ICP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}][\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{ICP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}][\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]</annotation></semantics></math> by one.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Next, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> sets <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{0}=(\rho_{n^{\prime}},\,\rho_{n^{\prime}-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{0}=(\rho_{n^{\prime}},\,\rho_{n^{\prime}-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and constructs:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}=(r_{1},\,\mathit{info}_{A_{I}},\,Q_{I,R},\,\Delta_{I,R},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{0})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑖𝑛𝑓𝑜</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}=(r_{1},\,\mathit{info}_{A_{I}},\,Q_{I,R},\,\Delta_{I,R},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{info}_{A_{I}}=(\mathit{Cert}^{ID}_{U_{I}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\,M_{A_{I}},\,\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ID},\,\sigma^{U_{I}}_{A_{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑖𝑛𝑓𝑜</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐶𝑒𝑟𝑡</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{info}_{A_{I}}=(\mathit{Cert}^{ID}_{U_{I}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\,M_{A_{I}},\,\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ID},\,\sigma^{U_{I}}_{A_{I}})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>’s own information,
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{I,R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{I,R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the interaction budget, and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{I,R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{I,R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the time budget.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> then signs <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> using a hash-based signature scheme:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{A_{I}}_{init}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{A_{I}}}(m_{0})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗀𝗇</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{A_{I}}_{init}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{A_{I}}}(m_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">and sends <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{0},\,\sigma^{\mathsf{TA}}_{ac},\,\sigma^{A_{I}}_{init},\,\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ICP})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>𝖳𝖠</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{0},\,\sigma^{\mathsf{TA}}_{ac},\,\sigma^{A_{I}}_{init},\,\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ICP})</annotation></semantics></math>
to <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ICP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ICP}</annotation></semantics></math> is the user’s signature on the policies defined in
the ICP. Finally, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> computes the session expiry time as
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}_{exp}=\tau_{now}+\Delta_{I,R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}_{exp}=\tau_{now}+\Delta_{I,R}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{now}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{now}</annotation></semantics></math> is the current time
and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{I,R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{I,R}</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum allowed session duration.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Verifying the first message.</span>
Agent <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{\mathsf{TA}}_{ac}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>𝖳𝖠</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{\mathsf{TA}}_{ac}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>’s signature using:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{\mathsf{TA}}}\!\bigl(\langle\nu,\,\mathit{Cert}^{ID}_{U_{R}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\,M_{A_{R}},\,\sigma^{U_{R}}_{ID},\,\sigma^{U_{R}}_{A_{R}}\rangle,\;\sigma^{\mathsf{TA}}_{ac}\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵𝖾𝗋𝗂𝖿𝗒</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>𝖳𝖠</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐶𝑒𝑟𝑡</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>𝖳𝖠</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{\mathsf{TA}}}\!\bigl(\langle\nu,\,\mathit{Cert}^{ID}_{U_{R}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\,M_{A_{R}},\,\sigma^{U_{R}}_{ID},\,\sigma^{U_{R}}_{A_{R}}\rangle,\;\sigma^{\mathsf{TA}}_{ac}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{A_{R}}}\!\bigl(m_{0},\;\sigma^{A_{I}}_{init}\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵𝖾𝗋𝗂𝖿𝗒</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{A_{R}}}\!\bigl(m_{0},\;\sigma^{A_{I}}_{init}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">If verification passes, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies the user’s signature on the ICP policy:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{U_{I}}}\!\bigl(\langle\rho_{n^{\prime}},\,n^{\prime}\rangle,\;\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ICP}\bigr)=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵𝖾𝗋𝗂𝖿𝗒</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{U_{I}}}\!\bigl(\langle\rho_{n^{\prime}},\,n^{\prime}\rangle,\;\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ICP}\bigr)=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p">It then checks that <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{0}=(\rho_{n^{\prime}},\,\rho_{n^{\prime}-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{0}=(\rho_{n^{\prime}},\,\rho_{n^{\prime}-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is
correct by verifying <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{n^{\prime}}=H(\rho_{n^{\prime}-1},\,n^{\prime},\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{n^{\prime}}=H(\rho_{n^{\prime}-1},\,n^{\prime},\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> initializes two counters, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{ICP}\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{ICP}\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{RCP}\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{RCP}\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, to track the number
of requests, setting each according to the policies of <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. It then
decrements <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{ICP}\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{ICP}\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]</annotation></semantics></math> by one.
It also checks the maximum time budget <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{R,I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R,I}</annotation></semantics></math> it is allowed to allocate
to <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> as determined in the RCP, and computes the session expiry time as
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{exp}=\tau_{now}+\Delta_{R,I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{exp}=\tau_{now}+\Delta_{R,I}</annotation></semantics></math>. It stores <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{exp}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{RCP}\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{RCP}\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]</annotation></semantics></math> as part of the session state.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> then generates a seed
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\,\mathit{addr})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖱𝖥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\,\mathit{addr})</annotation></semantics></math>
(where <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{addr}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{addr}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for the first chain) and builds a personalized hash
chain of length <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{R,I}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{R,I}=n</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{0},\quad s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{0},\quad s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H(s_{0},\,1,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(s_{0},\,1,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H(s_{1},\,2,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn> 2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(s_{1},\,2,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\vdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\vdots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p">It also obtains the user’s signature on the root of the chain:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U_{R}}_{RCP}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{U_{R}}}(s_{n},\,Q_{R,I})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗀𝗇</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U_{R}}_{RCP}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{U_{R}}}(s_{n},\,Q_{R,I})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Next, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> generates a random value <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and computes a session key
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{ses}=H(r_{1},\,r_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{ses}=H(r_{1},\,r_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, used throughout all communications with <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>
during the A-session. It constructs the response message:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}=(r_{2},\,Q_{R,I},\,\Delta_{R,I},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{1},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}=(r_{2},\,Q_{R,I},\,\Delta_{R,I},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{1},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{1}=\rho_{n^{\prime}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{1}=\rho_{n^{\prime}-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the token received from <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{1}=(s_{n},\,s_{n-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{1}=(s_{n},\,s_{n-1})</annotation></semantics></math> is the next token it has generated.
It computes an authentication tag <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{tag}_{1}=\mathsf{HMAC}_{k_{ses}}(m_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧𝖬𝖠𝖢</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{tag}_{1}=\mathsf{HMAC}_{k_{ses}}(m_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>
and sends <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{1},\,\sigma^{U_{R}}_{RCP},\,\mathit{tag}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑔</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{1},\,\sigma^{U_{R}}_{RCP},\,\mathit{tag}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> back to <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> decrements <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}][\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}][\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]</annotation></semantics></math>
by one and removes <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> from storage.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Transmission.</span>
After the handshake, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> exchange <span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p11.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">task-msg</span> protected under the
session key. Each message carries the next hash-chain token, allowing the
receiver to verify message authenticity, token progression, and compliance with
the remaining <span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p11.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">task-msg</span> and time budgets. The exchange continues until the task
ends, a budget is exhausted, or the session expires, and may span multiple
PQ-TLS sessions.
The steps during the transmission phase are:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>: Making request <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Agent <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies the response received in the previous round by checking:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{tag}_{i-1}==\mathsf{HMAC}_{k_{ses}}(m_{i-1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑔</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧𝖬𝖠𝖢</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{tag}_{i-1}==\mathsf{HMAC}_{k_{ses}}(m_{i-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{ses}=H(r_{1},r_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{ses}=H(r_{1},r_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}=(r_{2},\,\mathit{res}_{1},\,n,\,\Delta_{R,I},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{1},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{1},\,\sigma^{U_{R}}_{RCP})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑟𝑒𝑠</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}=(r_{2},\,\mathit{res}_{1},\,n,\,\Delta_{R,I},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{1},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{1},\,\sigma^{U_{R}}_{RCP})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=2</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. this is the first time <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> receives a response from <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,
it additionally verifies that <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{1}=\rho_{n^{\prime}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{1}=\rho_{n^{\prime}-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, checks
the user’s signature on the RCP:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{U_{R}}}\!\bigl(\langle s_{n},\,Q_{R,I}\rangle,\;\sigma^{U_{R}}_{RCP}\bigr)=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵𝖾𝗋𝗂𝖿𝗒</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{U_{R}}}\!\bigl(\langle s_{n},\,Q_{R,I}\rangle,\;\sigma^{U_{R}}_{RCP}\bigr)=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p">and verifies the chain link:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}=H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}=H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p13.3" class="ltx_p">It then checks <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{exp}\leq\tau^{\prime}_{now}+\Delta_{R,I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{exp}\leq\tau^{\prime}_{now}+\Delta_{R,I}</annotation></semantics></math>, initializes counter
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]=n</annotation></semantics></math>,
and decrements it by one.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> instead verifies that <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is correct
by checking:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-i+1}=H(s_{n-i},\,n-i+1,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-i+1}=H(s_{n-i},\,n-i+1,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p14.2" class="ltx_p">and that <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]=n-i+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]=n-i+1</annotation></semantics></math>, then decrements it by one.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p">In both cases, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> sets the next initiator token <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{i}=\rho_{n^{\prime}-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{i}=\rho_{n^{\prime}-i}</annotation></semantics></math>, removes <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{n^{\prime}-i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{n^{\prime}-i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, decrements
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{ICP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{ICP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]</annotation></semantics></math> by one,
and constructs and sends the following to <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}=(\mathit{req}_{i},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{i},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑟𝑒𝑞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}=(\mathit{req}_{i},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{i},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{tag}_{i}=\mathsf{HMAC}_{k_{ses}}(m_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑔</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧𝖬𝖠𝖢</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{tag}_{i}=\mathsf{HMAC}_{k_{ses}}(m_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p15.2" class="ltx_p">Note that if the PQ-TLS session was closed, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> first re-establishes a PQ-TLS
channel with <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> before sending. If
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}^{\prime}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies the chain seed:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\,\mathit{addr})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖱𝖥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\,\mathit{addr})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i+1</annotation></semantics></math>: Responding to request <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Agent <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> first checks that
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the quota <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{R,I}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{R,I}=n</annotation></semantics></math> has been reached, it returns a quota-exhausted message
and terminates the connection. It also checks that the session expiry time
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{exp}</annotation></semantics></math> has not been reached; if it has, it returns a session-expired message
and terminates the connection.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p">Otherwise, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies the tag and checks the next responder token:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{tag}_{i}==\mathsf{HMAC}_{k_{ses}}(m_{i}),\qquad\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{i}=s_{n-i+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑔</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧𝖬𝖠𝖢</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{tag}_{i}==\mathsf{HMAC}_{k_{ses}}(m_{i}),\qquad\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{i}=s_{n-i+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.2" class="ltx_p">If verification passes, <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> executes the request and constructs the response:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i+1}=(\mathit{res}_{i+1},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{i+1},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{i+1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑟𝑒𝑠</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i+1}=(\mathit{res}_{i+1},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{i+1},\,\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{tag}_{i+1}=\mathsf{HMAC}_{k_{ses}}(m_{i+1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑔</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧𝖬𝖠𝖢</mi><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{tag}_{i+1}=\mathsf{HMAC}_{k_{ses}}(m_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{i+1}=\rho_{n^{\prime}-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{NextTok}^{ICP}_{i+1}=\rho_{n^{\prime}-i}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{i+1}=s_{n-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑁𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑇𝑜𝑘</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{NextTok}^{RCP}_{i+1}=s_{n-i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and sends
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{i+1},\mathit{tag}_{i+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑡𝑎𝑔</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{i+1},\mathit{tag}_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. It then decrements both
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{ICP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{ICP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{RCP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]</annotation></semantics></math> by one,
and removes <math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. If
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{ICP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{ICP}[\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}]\allowbreak[\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS4.SSS2.p17.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies the chain seed:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\,\mathit{addr})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖱𝖥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\,\mathit{addr})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5. </span>Multi-Agent Intercommunication</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For tasks that involve multiple agents, the <span id="S4.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent receives the task and, under a static plan,
identifies the agents to contact. It generates the hash chains for the
collaborating agents in the <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session and sends the roots to the user, who builds
and signs a Merkle root over them and returns the tree and the signature to the
<span id="S4.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span>. Details are given in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D User-Agent Interaction for Multi-agent Setting ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.5.1. </span>Agent discovery.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Agent discovery protocol is similar to that for the two-agent protocol; it is run before the inter-agent communication and allows the <span id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent to receive a token from the <span id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> for each A-session that it wants to establish if it is authorized to contact other agents according to CP. The inter-agent communication stage handles the A-sessions that the <span id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent establishes with other agents according to the plan of the task. In each A-session RCP is determined by the receiving agent, and ICP is determined by the orchestrator agent (enforcing ICP in each session corresponds to enforcing an interaction budget and time budget in each A-session).
Agent <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> who wants to establish a connection with agent <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[1,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[1,t]</annotation></semantics></math>, first contacts the <span id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> to receive <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>’s information. Additionally, the <span id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> checks whether <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> is allowed to communicate with <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> (according to the contact policy) or not and sends the signed information of <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> is eligible (see Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.4.1. Agent discovery. ‣ 4.4. Agent-to-Agent Intercommunication ‣ 4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.5.2. </span><math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session protocol.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider that the <span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> communicates with agents <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{1},\cdots,A_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{1},\cdots,A_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> through established A-sessions according to the workflow to fulfill the given task. Each A-session has two policies <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="RCP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">RCP</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ICP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ICP</annotation></semantics></math> that are enforced by the (user and) agents involved in that A-session.
For efficiency of <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> computation in a <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session, a single user-signed Merkle root commits to the
initiator-side hash-chain roots of all planned component <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session. Each component
<math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session then uses its usual <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session authorization token together with the relevant
Merkle proof to show that it belongs to the user-authorized <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Establishing subroutine A-sessions with <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{A_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{j\in[1,t]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">∈</mo><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{j\in[1,t]}</annotation></semantics></math>. </span>
Agent <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> follows the A-session establishment protocol for the two-agent
setting described earlier, with the following differences.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">First, <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> uses the signature <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U^{*}}_{ICP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U^{*}}_{ICP}</annotation></semantics></math> and the personalized
hash chains obtained during the <span id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">User-agent interaction</span> protocol, rather
than generating new hash chains. These chains are defined as:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho^{i}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho^{i}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A^{*}_{I}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}},\,\mathit{addr})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖱𝖥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A^{*}_{I}},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}},\,\mathit{addr}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho^{i}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho^{i}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H(\rho^{i}_{0},\,1,\,\mathit{sid}_{j},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(\rho^{i}_{0},\,1,\,\mathit{sid}_{j},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho^{i}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho^{i}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H(\rho^{i}_{1},\,2,\,\mathit{sid}_{j},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mn> 2</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(\rho^{i}_{1},\,2,\,\mathit{sid}_{j},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\vdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\vdots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\rho^{i}_{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\rho^{i}_{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H(\rho^{i}_{n^{\prime}-1},\,n^{\prime},\,\mathit{sid}_{j},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(\rho^{i}_{n^{\prime}-1},\,n^{\prime},\,\mathit{sid}_{j},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[0,m-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[0,m-1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Second, when <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> sends its request together with <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U^{*}}_{ICP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U^{*}}_{ICP}</annotation></semantics></math>,
it also sends the Merkle root <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Mroot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑀𝑟𝑜𝑜𝑡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Mroot}</annotation></semantics></math> and provides a Merkle proof
showing that the tuple <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{i}_{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{i}_{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is included in the Merkle tree whose
root has been signed.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, when agent <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> handles the request, it verifies the correctness of
the Merkle proof. Throughout these communication rounds, <math id="S4.SS5.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> also
checks before each new request that the maximum allowed time specified in the
ICP has not been exceeded.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>A Formalization of MAGIQ  Properties</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we describe the security properties and proof sketch for MAGIQ. The complete proof is presented in Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Security Analysis ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1. </span>Security Properties</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MAGIQ provides the following security properties:
<br class="ltx_break">– <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Confidentiality.</span> The contents of <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">task-msg</span> exchanged between two entities remain private and are accessible only to the participating entities, except as revealed by the intended protocol outputs.
<br class="ltx_break">– <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Authentication.</span> All communications between entities are mutually authenticated at both the network and application layers.
<br class="ltx_break">– <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Message integrity.</span> <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Task-msg</span> exchanged between two entities are protected against unauthorized modification, forgery, replay, and re-ordering.
<br class="ltx_break">– <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Accountability.</span> <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Task-msg</span> are publicly verifiably attributable to their sender agent and, through the certification/binding mechanism, to the associated user.
<br class="ltx_break">– <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Authorization soundness.</span> No agent can interact with another agent unless authorized by its owner. The system enforces user-defined contact lists and <em id="S5.SS1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">budgets</em> on the number and duration of sessions, and on the number of <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">task-msg</span>, as specified by policy.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2. </span>Modeling MAGIQ in the UC Approach</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We model and analyze the security of MAGIQ using Canetti’s Universally
Composable (UC) framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Canetti, 2001</a>)</cite>. The UC framework captures the
security of a protocol <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> in a realistic setting where <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> may run
concurrently with other protocols, and where these protocols may interact with <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and with one another. More details about UC can be found in Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E UC Model and Ideal Functionalities ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.
We assume <em id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">static corruption</em>, where the adversary <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> corrupts
parties before protocol execution begins. This is a common simplifying assumption
in UC analyses <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dziembowski et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Canetti et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hesse et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 5.2. Modeling MAGIQ in the UC Approach ‣ 5. A Formalization of MAGIQ Properties ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> gives an outline of the MAGIQ ideal functionality and
the corresponding real-world construction, together with the auxiliary ideal
functionalities available to each. The ideal functionalities of <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session and <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session formalize the above security properties. See section <a href="#A5.SS8" title="E.8. Secure A-session Ideal Functionality ℱ_𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌 ‣ Appendix E UC Model and Ideal Functionalities ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.06933v1/figures/MAGIQModel2.jpg" id="S5.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:381/191;" width="381" height="191" alt="To avoid warning.">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>. </span><span id="S5.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The modular model of MAGIQ in the hybrid and ideal world.
The dotted box shows the ideal functionalities we have defined for MAGIQ and the gray boxes show the existing ideal functionalities used as subroutine in our model.</span><span id="acmlabel6" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">To avoid warning.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Modeling MAGIQ in ideal-world.</span> MAGIQ in the ideal world uses the <span id="S5.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">global random oracle functionality <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math></span> and the <span id="S5.SS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">global clock ideal functionality <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> as subroutines.
The former captures the assumptions of a synchronized global clock. Our analysis is in the <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>-hybrid model, and so the proof is in the UC global random-oracle model.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">MAGIQ consists of several protocols, whose security requirements are captured by corresponding ideal functionalities. These include the <span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">registration functionality <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>, modeling registration of users and agents with the <span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span>; the <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session-<span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">authorization functionality </span> <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}</annotation></semantics></math>, modeling <span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">agent discovery</span> with the help of <span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> that allows getting authorization to initiate an <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session; the <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-session functionality <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>, modeling authenticated inter-agent communication and policy enforcement in a two-agent session; and the <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-session functionality</span> <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}</annotation></semantics></math>, modeling the corresponding properties for a one-to-many agent session. The latter two functionalities interact with the global functionalities <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The functionalities <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S5.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}</annotation></semantics></math> capture, respectively, ideal registration and authorization by checking requests against an authorization table. Their details are given in Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E UC Model and Ideal Functionalities ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-session Ideal Functionality.</span>
The ideal functionality of an <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session, denoted by
<math id="S5.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>, captures a policy-enforced secure session
involving three types of entities: a user who provides the task and two agents that interact to perform the task. In addition to enforcing
the session policy, the functionality captures communication security guarantees, including message confidentiality, integrity, authenticity, and attribution to the sending agent. <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> has
access to the global clock functionality <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the
global random-oracle functionality <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-session Ideal Functionality.</span>
A <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session is a one-to-many agent session in which <span id="S5.SS2.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> distributes
its budget across multiple responders, enforcing its own
budget.
The ideal functionality of a <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session, denoted by
<math id="S5.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}</annotation></semantics></math>, captures communication security and attribution guarantees, analogous to those of an <math id="S5.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session, together with policy enforcement across all participating agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Modeling MAGIQ hybrid world.</span>
MAGIQ is analyzed using widely adopted UC functionalities as subroutines:
the global random oracle <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Camenisch et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, the global clock
<math id="S5.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Canetti et al., 2017</a>)</cite>, the secure communication-session functionality
<math id="S5.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gajek et al., 2008</a>)</cite>, and the certificate-authority functionality
<math id="S5.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Canetti, 2004</a>)</cite>. MAGIQ consists of several protocols
including registration, agent discovery, <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session, and <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session. An <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session uses
<math id="S5.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a post-quantum adaptation of the TLS secure
session functionality with security considered against quantum
polynomial-time adversaries and environments, may span multiple PQ-TLS sessions, and relies on
<math id="S5.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math> for certificate-based trust. A <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session is realized by
the one-to-many MAGIQ protocol using multiple instances of
<math id="S5.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with access to <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S5.SS2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3. </span>Security Proof Sketch</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We analyze MAGIQ in the UC framework; the following theorem gives the security of our protocol:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Theorem 5.1.</h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">MAGIQ  (Section <a href="#S4" title="4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) UC-realizes
<math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the
<math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>-hybrid model.
The cryptographic building blocks of MAGIQ are (i) a digital signature scheme that is EUF-CMA, and (ii) hash function, HMAC and PRF that are modeled by global random oracles.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">(It is sufficient for the signature scheme that are used by all MAGIQ participants to be EUF-CMA in the standard model (see proof <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Security Analysis ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>)).</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof sketch.</h5>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We construct the protocol
<math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{MAGIQ}^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{MAGIQ}^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>-hybrid model and prove Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1. ‣ 5.3. Security Proof Sketch ‣ 5. A Formalization of MAGIQ Properties ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> through a sequence of lemmas, each capturing the security of one protocol in MAGIQ. These protocols are executed sequentially: an agent may participate in an <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session or a <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session only after registration, and an initiating agent may start the session only after obtaining authorization from the <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span>. The lemmas are stated below; full details are given in Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Security Analysis ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma 5.2.</h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The registration protocol <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{Reg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{Reg}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}</annotation></semantics></math> for the user and the agent, described in Appendix <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>, UC realizes the registration ideal functionality <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}</annotation></semantics></math> against static adversaries.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof sketch.</span> The user and the <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> are honest. The simulator <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> produces
outputs for the honest parties that are consistent with the ideal registration functionality: <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> generates the required key pairs and
simulates the CA interaction consistent with
<math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the simulated registration transcript with the <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> and the
certificates are distributed identically to those in the hybrid execution, no
environment can distinguish the ideal execution from the hybrid execution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma 5.3.</h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session- agent discovery and authorization protocol <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{MAGIQ}^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{MAGIQ}^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> described in Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4. Agent-to-Agent Intercommunication ‣ 4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> UC-realizes the <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session-authorization ideal
functionality <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}</annotation></semantics></math> against static adversaries.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof sketch.</span>
The simulator <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> runs the registration simulator described in previous Lemma, maintaining a consistent registration state. If
<math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> are honest, the authorization request and response are
generated honestly and consistently with <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> is corrupted, <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> receives the request that <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> causes <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> to send, checks it against the registration state and authorization table, and returns the corresponding
provider response or rejection.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma 5.4.</h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session protocol <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{Ases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{Ases}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{MAGIQ}^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}},\mathcal{F}_{CA},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{MAGIQ}^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}},\mathcal{F}_{CA},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> (described in Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4. Agent-to-Agent Intercommunication ‣ 4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>) UC realizes the <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session ideal functionality <math id="S5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> against static adversaries.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof sketch.</span>
<math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> uses the registration and authorization simulators to maintain consistent view for registration and authorization tokens and
policies, and simulates the <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session handshake and message
transmission. If both agents are honest, <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> relays the session messages to <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> and delivers the outputs prescribed by <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> that enforces policies.
If one agent is corrupted, <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> obtains adversarially chosen messages of that agent through
<math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, checks the authorization token, user and agent signatures, HMAC tags, hash-chain token progression using <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the message/time budgets using <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Invalid messages cause <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> sends abort to <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In-distinguishability </span> follows from the EUF-CMA security of the signature scheme against quantum polynomial-time adversaries, and the seudorandomness/unforgeability provided by the HMAC, PRF, and hash-chain checks in the <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> model.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma 5.5.</h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session protocol <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{Cses}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{Cses}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}},\mathcal{F}_{CA},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}},\mathcal{F}_{CA},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}</annotation></semantics></math> (described in Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4. Agent-to-Agent Intercommunication ‣ 4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>) UC realizes the <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session ideal functionality <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}</annotation></semantics></math> against static adversaries assuming that <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{Ases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{Ases}</annotation></semantics></math> UC realizes <math id="S5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof sketch.</span> We consider three cases: (i) all agents are honest, (ii) only <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is corrupted, and (iii) all <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are corrupted. In all cases <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates each <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In case (ii), <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> receives the subtasks for each <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> from the corrupted <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and simulates <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> accordingly, but in case (i) and (iii), <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> receives the task from the dummy <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and it runs the task internally and gets the subtasks for each <math id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> that it will simulate.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6. </span>Experimental Results</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we present experimental results.
We measure the overhead of MAGIQ
across cryptographic operations, protocol coordination, network
communication, and bandwidth. We further evaluate MAGIQ in a
multi-agent setting where an initiating agent coordinates with multiple
receiving agents to complete a task.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1. </span>Setup</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Libraries.</span> We use XMSS_SHA2_16_256 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huelsing et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, an instance of XMSS using SHA-256, a Winternitz parameter of 16, and a 256-bit security level, to instantiate long-term agent identity keys. All inter-agent and agent–<span id="S6.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> communication is secured via post-quantum mutually authenticated TLS (PQ-mTLS), configured with X25519 and ML-KEM-768 for hybrid key exchange, ML-DSA-65 for transport-layer certificates and mutual authentication, and TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 as the cipher suite. The PQ-mTLS stack is implemented using OpenSSL 3.5, while post-quantum cryptographic primitives are provided via the liboqs-python library. SHA-256 serves as the hash function across all protocol operations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Agents. </span>The LLM agents were implemented using AutoGen <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. For comparison with the experimental evaluation of SAGA, we used gpt-4.1, gpt-4.1-mini, and locally hosted Qwen2.5-72B. In addition, we evaluated other cloud-hosted OpenAI models such as gpt-5.4, gpt-5.4-mini and locally deployed Qwen3.5-30B-Instruct to assess performance across a broader range of configurations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Device Specifications. </span>Experiments were conducted on Ubuntu 24.04, running on an AMD Ryzen Threadripper PRO 5955WX with 16 cores and 256 GB of RAM, with all reported results averaged over 100 runs. The Qwen 30B Instruct model ran on an NVIDIA RTX 4090 while Qwen-2.5 72B model used an NVIDIA H100. For all experiments, the user and the agents they own were assumed to reside on the same device.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline.</span> We use SAGA as the baseline protocol. All cryptographic operations in SAGA are built on Curve25519, with both long-term and ephemeral keys generated via the X25519 ECDH scheme using 256-bit shared secrets. Certificates follow the X.509 PKI standard and are issued by an internal certificate authority deployed as part of the <span id="S6.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span>, with SHA-256 used for all digital signatures and key derivation. Cryptographic primitives were implemented using the cryptography library in Python 3.12. We used the LLM agents that came with the SAGA distribution, implemented using the <span id="S6.SS1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">smolagents</span> library. Experiments were conducted with a local Qwen-2.5 72B model on an NVIDIA H100, as well as cloud-hosted OpenAI models accessed via API. The code for SAGA was obtained from the github repo <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">gsiros, 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2. </span>Computation Overhead</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 6.2. Computation Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> reports the computational overhead of protocol operations in MAGIQ against the SAGA baseline.
Note that for SAGA, user registration, agent registration, and the setup phases on both the initiating and receiving agents are analogous to the respective handshake phases in MAGIQ. Notably, SAGA does not include counterparts to the Handshake Phase (User) or Contact Resolution (Initiating) phase, as user involvement is not required during the handshake, and contact resolution is subsumed within the setup phase of the initiating agent. As reflected in Table <a href="#S6.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 6.2. Computation Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the token decryption and validation for SAGA are incorporated into the per-interaction data transfer costs on the initiating agent, with token validation similarly accounted for on the receiving agent. Token generation by the initiating agent is likewise subsumed within its handshake phase, rather than treated as a separate operation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On the user side, both user and agent registration in MAGIQ incur <math id="S6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>36 seconds, attributable to XMSS key tree pre-computation. This cost is paid only once at deployment. <span id="S6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span>-side registration, by contrast, takes at most 5.4 ms, confirming that post-quantum key management imposes no scalability burden on the infrastructure side.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Recurring per-session costs in MAGIQ remain uniformly sub-5 ms across all operations. Contact resolution, handshake phases across all three roles, and data transfer together constitute a modest operational footprint. Data transfer in MAGIQ is effectively free at 0.03 ms per interaction, compared to 1.44 ms on the initiating side in SAGA— a reduction of nearly two orders of magnitude.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T1" class="ltx_table">
