<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3. </span>Protocol Overhead</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the overhead introduced by the access control and <span id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> coordination mechanisms of MAGIQ compared with SAGA. We consider a
scenario in which an initiating agent <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>  issues <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> requests to a
receiving agent <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, subject to a maximum of <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> requests per
<math id="S6.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-sessionbetween <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>  and <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. The total overhead comprises both a
network component, associated with establishing secure communication, and
a cryptographic component, denoted <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\mathrm{crypto}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>crypto</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\mathrm{crypto}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which captures
the costs of all phases involved in agent communication and data transfer,
as detailed in Table <a href="#S6.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 6.2. Computation Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. The total protocol overhead
is modeled as:</p>
<table id="S6.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{proto}}(m)=\bigl(\mathrm{RTT}_{A_{i},P}+t_{\text{crypto}}\bigr)\cdot\left\lceil\frac{m}{Q_{\max}}\right\rceil," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>proto</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>RTT</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>crypto</mtext></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{proto}}(m)=\bigl(\mathrm{RTT}_{A_{i},P}+t_{\text{crypto}}\bigr)\cdot\left\lceil\frac{m}{Q_{\max}}\right\rceil,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is the <span id="S6.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> and <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{RTT}_{A_{i},P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>RTT</mi><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{RTT}_{A_{i},P}</annotation></semantics></math> is the round-trip
time between <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>  and the <span id="S6.SS3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span>. <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{crypto}}=20.33" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>crypto</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20.33</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{crypto}}=20.33</annotation></semantics></math> ms is
the measured cryptographic overhead per <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session. Each authorization cycle
must be performed once every <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> requests.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We sample round-trip times from empirical measurement distributions using
monitors in US-East, US-West, Europe, and Asia, made available by
CAIDA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">CAIDA, </a>)</cite> and AWS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Adorjan, 2025</a>)</cite>. Figures <a href="#S6.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 6.3. Protocol Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>
and <a href="#S6.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 6.3. Protocol Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> show the amortized protocol
overhead:</p>
<table id="S6.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{c}_{\text{proto}}(m)=\frac{c_{\text{proto}}(m)}{m}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>c</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>proto</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>proto</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{c}_{\text{proto}}(m)=\frac{c_{\text{proto}}(m)}{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">as a function of <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, using <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=100</annotation></semantics></math> requests, under two
configurations: one in which the <span id="S6.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> location varies
across four geographic regions while agents are distributed worldwide
(Fig. <a href="#S6.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 6.3. Protocol Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), and one in which the
<span id="S6.SS3.p2.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> is fixed in US-West while the initiating agent <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>  is placed
across the same four regions
(Fig. <a href="#S6.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 6.3. Protocol Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F7" class="ltx_figure">
