<section id="S6.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.5. </span>Performance Evaluation of Provider</h3>

<div id="S6.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the cumulative overhead imposed on the <span id="S6.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> as a function
of <math id="S6.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session  lifetime, varying the number of initiating agents. Because
each new <math id="S6.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session  requires one contact-resolution operation at the
<span id="S6.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> (2.96 ms, Table <a href="#S6.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 6.2. Computation Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), a shorter session
lifetime increases the rate at which this operation must be performed and
thus the total <span id="S6.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> burden. For <math id="S6.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> initiating agents each
refreshing sessions of lifetime <math id="S6.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> minutes, the daily overhead is:</p>
<table id="S6.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{{Provider} }}(n,\ell)=n\cdot\frac{1440}{\ell}\cdot t_{\text{crypto}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Provider</mtext><mtext> </mtext></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1440</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>crypto</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{{Provider} }}(n,\ell)=n\cdot\frac{1440}{\ell}\cdot t_{\text{crypto}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{crypto}}=2.96" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>crypto</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.96</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{crypto}}=2.96</annotation></semantics></math> ms is the measured contact-resolution
cost and <math id="S6.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1440" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1440</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1440</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of minutes in a day. Compared with SAGA,
which incurs a contact-resolution cost of 1.46 ms per-session,
MAGIQ introduces approximately <math id="S6.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times</annotation></semantics></math> the per-session <span id="S6.SS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> cost, owing to its additional post-quantum cryptographic operations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S6.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ 6.5. Performance Evaluation of Provider ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> plots <math id="S6.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{{Provider} }}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Provider</mtext><mtext> </mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{{Provider} }}</annotation></semantics></math>
for <math id="S6.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\{1,10,100\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\{1,10,100\}</annotation></semantics></math> agents across session lifetimes ranging from
one minute to one day. Two structural observations follow directly from
Equation <a href="#S6.E3" title="In 6.5. Performance Evaluation of Provider ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. First, overhead scales linearly with
agent count: the 100-agent curve lies exactly one order of magnitude above
the 10-agent curve at every point. Second, overhead is inversely
proportional to session lifetime: moving from a 1-minute to a 1-day
session reduces <span id="S6.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> cost by three orders of magnitude for any fixed
agent population. Even accounting for the <math id="S6.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times</annotation></semantics></math> increase in
per-session cost relative to SAGA, the absolute <span id="S6.SS5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> burden remains
negligible across all evaluated configurations, confirming that the
post-quantum overhead of MAGIQ does not materially alter the
scalability characteristics of the system.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.06933v1/provider_overhead_session.svg" id="S6.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/191;" width="286" height="191" aria-label="To avoid warning."><p>To avoid warning.</p></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>. </span><span id="S6.F9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Computational overhead on the <span id="S6.F9.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> as a function
of <math id="S6.F9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-sessionlifetime, for 1, 10, and 100 initiating agents.
</span><span id="acmlabel9" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">To avoid warning.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.6. </span>Bandwidth Overhead</h3>

<div id="S6.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 6.6. Bandwidth Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> summarizes the bandwidth requirements across protocol phases for SAGA and MAGIQ. For SAGA, we assume <math id="S6.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=100</annotation></semantics></math> one-time keys (OTKs) are registered by the user on behalf of the agent. For both protocols, we consider a setting in which an initiating agent <math id="S6.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>  issues <math id="S6.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=10</annotation></semantics></math> requests to a receiving agent <math id="S6.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, with a maximum of <math id="S6.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\max}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\max}=10</annotation></semantics></math> requests per <math id="S6.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">User and agent registration incur one-time costs and therefore do not affect per-task bandwidth. In SAGA, these costs amount to 0.6 KB for user registration and 10.40 KB for agent registration, whereas in MAGIQ they increase to 6.98 KB and 27.28 KB, respectively. The most significant difference arises during session establishment, which constitutes the recurring per-token-cycle overhead: SAGA requires 2.12 KB per cycle, while MAGIQ incurs 88.65 KB, representing a <math id="S6.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>42<math id="S6.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> increase. The bulk of this overhead is due to the post quantum certificates and signatures being transmitted in between <math id="S6.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>  and <math id="S6.SS6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>  during the handshake phase. In contrast, per-request data transfer remains comparable between the two protocols, at 0.59 KB for SAGA and 0.56 KB for MAGIQ. When using MAGIQ for tasks involving more than 2 agents, only the bandwidth required for the agent communication phase grows linearly with the number of agents. Specifically, with <math id="S6.SS6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> agents the cost scales <math id="S6.SS6.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(t-1)\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t-1)\times</annotation></semantics></math> the per session bandwidth.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>. </span><span id="S6.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Bandwidth requirements (in KB) per protocol phase for SAGA and MAGIQ. SAGA parameters: <math id="S6.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=100</annotation></semantics></math> OTKs,
<math id="S6.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=10</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\max}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\max}=10</annotation></semantics></math>. MAGIQ parameters: <math id="S6.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=10</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S6.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\max}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\max}=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S6.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Operation</span></th>
<th id="S6.T4.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">SAGA</span></th>
<th id="S6.T4.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">MAGIQ</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T4.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T4.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">User Registration</span></td>
<td id="S6.T4.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.6</span></td>
<td id="S6.T4.5.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">6.98</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T4.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T4.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Agent Registration</span></td>
<td id="S6.T4.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">10.40</span></td>
<td id="S6.T4.5.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">27.28</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T4.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T4.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Agent Communication (per session)</span></td>
<td id="S6.T4.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">2.12</span></td>
<td id="S6.T4.5.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">88.65</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T4.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T4.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Data Transfer (per request)</span></td>
<td id="S6.T4.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.59</span></td>
<td id="S6.T4.5.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T4.5.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.56</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.7. </span>One-Agent to Many-Agents Overhead</h3>

<div id="S6.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the overhead borne by an <span id="S6.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> (<math id="S6.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>) that
coordinates with <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> receiving agents to complete a task.
For each receiving agent <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>  must establish one <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session 
comprising a contact-resolution step and a handshake phase.
We assume all <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-sessions share the same lifetime <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> and that
each <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session  comprises <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{max}</annotation></semantics></math>=10 requests.
The per-session cryptographic cost on <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>  is:</p>
<table id="S6.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\text{init}}(t)=\underbrace{4.1\,t}_{\text{contact resolution}}+\underbrace{4.01\,t}_{\text{handshake}}=8.11\,t\quad\text{(ms)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>init</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>4.1</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>contact resolution</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>4.01</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>handshake</mtext></munder></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8.11</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(ms)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\text{init}}(t)=\underbrace{4.1\,t}_{\text{contact resolution}}+\underbrace{4.01\,t}_{\text{handshake}}=8.11\,t\quad\text{(ms)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where costs are taken from Table <a href="#S6.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 6.2. Computation Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Because a new session must be established every <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> minutes,
the total daily overhead on <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>  is:</p>
<table id="S6.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{init}}(t,\,\ell)=c_{\text{init}}(t)\cdot\frac{1440}{\ell}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>init</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>init</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1440</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{init}}(t,\,\ell)=c_{\text{init}}(t)\cdot\frac{1440}{\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS7.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with 1440 denoting the number of minutes in a day.
Figure <a href="#S6.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ 6.7. One-Agent to Many-Agents Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> plots <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{init}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>init</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{init}}</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="S6.SS7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,2,5,10,15\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,2,5,10,15\}</annotation></semantics></math> across session lifetimes ranging from
one minute to one day.
The overhead is governed by two independent axes.
At a fixed lifetime, cost scales linearly with <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>: at a 1-minute
session lifetime, overhead ranges from <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>12 seconds for <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="S6.SS7.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>175 seconds for <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=15</annotation></semantics></math>, a 15<math id="S6.SS7.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> ratio consistent with
Equation <a href="#S6.E4" title="In 6.7. One-Agent to Many-Agents Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
At a fixed <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, cost falls inversely with <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>: for <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=15</annotation></semantics></math>,
extending the session lifetime from 1 minute to 1 hour reduces
daily overhead from <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>175 seconds to under 3 seconds, and to
under 0.4 seconds at 8 hours or beyond.
For all values of <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the curves converge to negligible overhead
beyond a 1-hour lifetime, confirming that session lifetime is the
dominant design parameter and that MAGIQ imposes no meaningful
burden on <math id="S6.SS7.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>  under practical deployment conditions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F10" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2605.06933v1/oh_initiating_mas.svg" id="S6.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/191;" width="286" height="191" aria-label="To avoid warnings."><p>To avoid warnings.</p></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>. </span><span id="S6.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Daily computational overhead on <math id="S6.F10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>  as a function of
<math id="S6.F10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session  lifetime, for <math id="S6.F10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,2,5,10,15\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,2,5,10,15\}</annotation></semantics></math> receiving agents.
Per-session cost follows Equation <a href="#S6.E4" title="In 6.7. One-Agent to Many-Agents Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> using measured
cryptographic costs; daily overhead follows
Equation <a href="#S6.E5" title="In 6.7. One-Agent to Many-Agents Overhead ‣ 6. Experimental Results ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
All <math id="S6.F10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-sessions are assumed to share the same lifetime.</span><span id="acmlabel10" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">To avoid warnings.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.8. </span>Multi-Agent Task Completion Overhead</h3>

