<td id="A2.T6.5.56.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T6.5.56.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The request execution function</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T6.5.57" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T6.5.57.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><math id="A2.T6.m72" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ExeRes()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ExeRes()</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A2.T6.5.57.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A2.T6.5.57.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The response execution function</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Cryptographic Enforcement of Policies</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below we define each of the three policies of CP, RCP, and ICP and give the mechanisms that are used to enforce each of them in our protocol.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1. </span>Contact Policy <math id="A3.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CP</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Users define and administer contact policies for their registered agents. The contact policy <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CP</annotation></semantics></math> states that which agents can establish a connection with whom and for how many times (budget). <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CP</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a set of declarative rules such as ("receive, *@company.com:email-agent", 10) which allows an email handling agent from a specified domain to initiate contact at most 10 times, or ("send, *@company.com:email-agent", 20) which allows the agent to initiate an A-session with an email handling agent for 20 times. If multiple rules match, the one with the highest specificity is selected. The number of connections between an initiating agent <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and responding agent <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the budget, is defined as below:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Budget(aid_{A_{R}},aid_{A_{I}})=\Bigg\{\begin{tabular}[]{l l}$-1$&amp;if $R=\emptyset$\\
$B(r^{*})$&amp;if $R\neq\emptyset$\end{tabular}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtable class="ltx_guessed_headers" columnspacing="4.0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_th_row" columnalign="left"><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_th_row" columnalign="left"><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Budget(aid_{A_{R}},aid_{A_{I}})=\Bigg\{\begin{tabular}[]{l l}$-1$&amp;if $R=\emptyset$\\
$B(r^{*})$&amp;if $R\neq\emptyset$\end{tabular}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Which state that <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the most specific rule among all rules <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\in CP_{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\in CP_{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> are establishing an A-session, and <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(r^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(r^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the rule <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> allows the user to distinguish between no match in policy and an expired budget.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Enforcing the contact policy <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CP</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> when an initiating agent <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> queries the provider to contact <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the provider first verifies that the agents participating in the A-session satisfy the contact policy <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CP_{A_{R}}\cap CP_{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CP_{A_{R}}\cap CP_{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means that <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CP_{A_{R}}\cap CP_{A_{I}}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CP_{A_{R}}\cap CP_{A_{I}}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. If this is the first time <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> connects, then the provider creates a counter <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Counter[aid_{A_{R}}][aid_{A_{I}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Counter[aid_{A_{R}}][aid_{A_{I}}]</annotation></semantics></math> to keep track of the number of contacts and initializes it with <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Min\{Budget(aid_{A_{R}},aid_{A_{I}}),Budget(aid_{A_{R}},aid_{A_{I}})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Min\{Budget(aid_{A_{R}},aid_{A_{I}}),Budget(aid_{A_{R}},aid_{A_{I}})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">If the policy check succeeds, the provider returns a signature <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{TA}_{ac}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{TA}_{ac}</annotation></semantics></math> to agent <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> on the recipient’s data and decreases the counter by one: <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{TA}_{ac}=HS.Sign_{sk_{TA}}(\nu,Cert^{ID}_{U_{R}},aid_{A_{R}},M_{A_{R}},\sigma^{U_{R}}_{ID},\sigma^{U_{R}}_{A_{R}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{TA}_{ac}=HS.Sign_{sk_{TA}}(\nu,Cert^{ID}_{U_{R}},aid_{A_{R}},M_{A_{R}},\sigma^{U_{R}}_{ID},\sigma^{U_{R}}_{A_{R}})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is a nonce used to ensure token freshness. We assume the receiver agent will keep track of the nonce. If <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Budget" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Budget</annotation></semantics></math> is negative, or exhausted, then provider sends a failure message and terminates the connection.
The user of agent <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> can update the contact policy and dedicate a new budget at any time.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2. </span>Responder Contact Policy <math id="A3.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="RCP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">RCP</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider RCP is defined by the user for a responding agent <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and consists of the tuples of the form <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{R},A_{I},Q_{R,I},\Delta_{R,I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{R},A_{I},Q_{R,I},\Delta_{R,I})</annotation></semantics></math> which states that in an A-session between <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the maximum number of requests that <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> can receive is <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{R,I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{R,I}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the maximum duration of the A-session is <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{R,I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R,I}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Enforcing the interaction budget in <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="RCP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">RCP</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> We assume the responding agent can be corrupted and define a scheme which allows the responding agent to keep the total budget counting correctly, while it ensures the budget has indeed been determined by the user, and the initiating agent can <span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">efficiently</span> verify when the responding agent exceed the maximum allowed budget.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> establishes an A-session with <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the responder agent
<math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> derives a random seed:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\;\mathit{addr})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖱𝖥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\;\mathit{addr})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{addr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{addr}</annotation></semantics></math> is the chain index for this A-session (set to <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>
for the first chain). It then builds a <em id="A3.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">personalized hash chain</em> of
length <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=Q_{R,I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=Q_{R,I}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{j}=H(s_{j-1},\;j,\;\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}),\qquad j=1,\ldots,n" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}=H(s_{j-1},\;j,\;\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}),\qquad j=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Binding <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> into each step prevents a corrupted <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>
from reusing the chain with another agent to exceed <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{R,I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{R,I}</annotation></semantics></math>; binding
<math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{sid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{sid}</annotation></semantics></math> prevents reuse across A-sessions; and the index <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> allows
<math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> to track which hash values <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> opens and detect any point of
cheating. These values serve as <em id="A3.I1.i1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hash-based message count tokens</em>
that enforce the interaction budget. Agent <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> then sends the terminal
value <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> to the user <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">User <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> signs the terminal value and chain length:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U_{R}}_{\mathit{RCP}}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{U_{R}}}(s_{n},\;Q_{R,I})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝑅𝐶𝑃</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗀𝗇</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U_{R}}_{\mathit{RCP}}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{U_{R}}}(s_{n},\;Q_{R,I})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and sends <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U_{R}}_{\mathit{RCP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝑅𝐶𝑃</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U_{R}}_{\mathit{RCP}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Agent <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> forwards <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{R,I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{R,I}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{R,I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{R,I}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U_{R}}_{\mathit{RCP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝑅𝐶𝑃</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U_{R}}_{\mathit{RCP}}</annotation></semantics></math> to the initiator <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Agent <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies the user’s signature:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{U_{R}}}\!\left(\langle\,s_{n},\;Q_{R,I}\,\rangle,\;\sigma^{U_{R}}_{\mathit{RCP}}\right)=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵𝖾𝗋𝗂𝖿𝗒</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝑅𝐶𝑃</mi><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{U_{R}}}\!\left(\langle\,s_{n},\;Q_{R,I}\,\rangle,\;\sigma^{U_{R}}_{\mathit{RCP}}\right)=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and checks that <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{R,I}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{R,I}=n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}})=s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}})=s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. If all checks pass, <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> is assured that
<math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> has correctly initialized the interaction budget, and initializes a
counter <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{\mathit{RCP}}=Q_{R,I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mi>𝑅𝐶𝑃</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{\mathit{RCP}}=Q_{R,I}</annotation></semantics></math>, decrementing it by one.
In subsequent rounds, each time <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> receives a token it verifies:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}=H(s_{i-1},\;i,\;\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}=H(s_{i-1},\;i,\;\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and decrements <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{\mathit{RCP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mi>𝑅𝐶𝑃</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{\mathit{RCP}}</annotation></semantics></math>. When the counter reaches
zero, <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> performs a final check:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\;\mathit{addr})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖱𝖥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{I}},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{R}},\;\mathit{addr})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">At this point <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> must cease accepting further requests; an honest <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>
will stop sending them regardless, though a corrupted <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> may not comply.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We guarantee that if both agents that are involved in an A-session are honest or only one of them is honest then the interaction budget will be correctly enforced. Note that we do not ensure any guarantee for the case when both agents are corrupted.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3. </span>Initiator Contact Policy <math id="A3.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ICP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ICP</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume that the user chooses <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{tot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{tot}</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, the maximum number of requests for an initiator agent that can send to other agents toward fulfilling a task, and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{tot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{tot}</annotation></semantics></math> that is the maximum duration of time that an initiator agent can interact with other agents to fulfill a given task. These two values are stored as the Initiator contact policy <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ICP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ICP</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ICP=(Q_{tot},\Delta_{tot})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ICP=(Q_{tot},\Delta_{tot})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Enforcing the interaction budget in <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ICP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ICP</annotation></semantics></math> (static workflow).</span> We assume that the <span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> acts as an initiator and orchestrates the communication with other agents <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},A_{2},\cdots,A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},A_{2},\cdots,A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> through sessions <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1},S_{2},...,S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1},S_{2},...,S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. We design a scheme that enforces the total budget <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{tot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{tot}</annotation></semantics></math> throughout all these sessions that allows <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> to keep the total budget counting correctly while ensuring that the budget has indeed been determined by user <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, the responding agents
<math id="A3.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, …., can <span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">efficiently</span> identify when <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds the budget without knowing the history of interactions of <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> with other agents and without interacting with other agents (just using their local views). We require that the communication should stay almost constant (independent of the request number) for each pair of agents.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We note that a single hash chain of length <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{tot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{tot}</annotation></semantics></math> will not work for <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ICP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ICP</annotation></semantics></math> since the agents need to know the history of the consumed hash tokens in order to verify the token presentations. This will also lead to a communication cost that grows linearly with the number of requests. Therefore, this naive approach will not work. To circumvent around this, we first consider that the agents follow an static workflow where the <span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent knows which agents it has to contact to fulfill the task as soon as it receives the task. We design the hash-based tokens to enforce the interaction budget for an static workflow as below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The user <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> determines the maximum interaction budget <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{tot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{tot}</annotation></semantics></math>
for <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ICP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ICP}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving a task from <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, agent <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> processes it and
obtains the workflow, identifying the list of agents <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},\ldots,A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},\ldots,A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>
to contact. It then creates <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> personalized hash chains of length <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>,
where each chain is seeded as:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A^{*}_{I}},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}},\;\mathit{addr})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖱𝖥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A^{*}_{I}},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}},\;\mathit{addr})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and extended as <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}=H(s_{j-1},\,j,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}=H(s_{j-1},\,j,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>. The parameters satisfy
<math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{tot}=n\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{tot}=n\times m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq t</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring the total chain length
does not exceed <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{tot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{tot}</annotation></semantics></math> and that at least one chain is available per
A-session; <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> may allocate two or more chains to a single A-session.
Agent <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> then sends the terminal values <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{n},s^{\prime}_{n},\ldots,s^{\ell}_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{n},s^{\prime}_{n},\ldots,s^{\ell}_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> of all personalized hash chains to user <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The user <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> constructs a Merkle tree over the terminal values and
signs the root together with the chain length:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{U^{*}}}(\mathit{Mroot},\;n)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗀𝗇</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑀𝑟𝑜𝑜𝑡</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{U^{*}}}(\mathit{Mroot},\;n),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and sends the Merkle tree and signature <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> initiates an A-session with agent <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[1,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[1,t]</annotation></semantics></math>,
it sends to <math id="A3.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A3.I2.i4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the Merkle root <math id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Mroot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑀𝑟𝑜𝑜𝑡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Mroot}</annotation></semantics></math> and user signature
<math id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">a Merkle proof that the hash chain root is included in the tree
signed by <math id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the chain openings <math id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A3.I2.i4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}=H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}=H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Agent <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies the following:</p>
<ul id="A3.I2.i5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the user’s signature: <math id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{U^{*}}}(\langle\mathit{Mroot},\,n\rangle,\,\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵𝖾𝗋𝗂𝖿𝗒</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝑀𝑟𝑜𝑜𝑡</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{U^{*}}}(\langle\mathit{Mroot},\,n\rangle,\,\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}})=1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the Merkle proof is valid</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the hash step: <math id="A3.I2.i5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}=H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}=H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.I2.i5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If all checks pass, <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is assured that <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> has authorized the use of
a personalized hash chain of length <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> for agent <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to fulfill the
task. Agent <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> then initializes a counter <math id="A3.I2.i5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{\mathit{ICP}}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{\mathit{ICP}}=n</annotation></semantics></math> and decrements it by one.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In the next rounds, the initiator agent just sends a hash token from the chain <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the responding agent <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies that <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}=H(s_{j-1},j,sid,aid_{A_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}=H(s_{j-1},j,sid,aid_{A_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and then decreases the counter <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ctr_{ICP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ctr_{ICP}</annotation></semantics></math>. When the counter <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ctr_{ICP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ctr_{ICP}</annotation></semantics></math> reaches 0 it checks that <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=PRF(sid,aid_{A^{*}_{I}},aid_{A_{i}},addr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=PRF(sid,aid_{A^{*}_{I}},aid_{A_{i}},addr)</annotation></semantics></math>. If the agent wants to continue interactions and use more hash chains, it can increment <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="addr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">addr</annotation></semantics></math> by 1, and repeat the last two steps mentioned above to start using a new personalized hash chain.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Enforcing the interaction budget in <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ICP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ICP</annotation></semantics></math> (dynamic workflow).</span>
For a dynamic workflow, the <span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent cannot know the list of agents who wants to contact with them ahead of time. Therefore, it cannot allocate the hash chains to the responding agents and create personalized hash chains from beginning. To solve this issue, the naive approach will be to let the <span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent to create the chains as soon as it finds with whom it has to contact. For example, if it initially learns that it has to contact with <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, it generates two or more hash chains of length <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, and sends the root of these personalized hash chain to user to sign. The user generates a Merkle tree on top of the hash chain terminal values and signs the Merkle root, and sends the Merkle tree and the signature to agent <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. Every time the agent creates a new hash chain, the user updates its Merkle tree and its signature.
This approach, however, is not efficient and requires too many interactions between the <span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent and the user.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Below, we give a more efficient scheme that allows the ICP to be enforced for a dynamic workflow (plan) with minimal interactions with the user. The idea is that user creates <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> one time signature (OTS) key pairs and generate a Merkle tree on the OTS public keys. Then, it signs the root of the Merkle tree, and sends the Merkle tree to the <span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent together with delegating the OTS private keys to the <span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent. On receiving these keys, the <span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent can generate personalized hash chains for any agent <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and it can plug in the hash chain to the Merkle tree by signing the terminal values of the hash chain using the delegated private keys. See below for more details.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">One time signature (OTS)</span> is a digital signature scheme that allows using a private and public key pair to sign a message only once. The examples of OTS are Lamport signature scheme <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lamport, 1979</a>)</cite>, and WOTS+ signature scheme <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Buchmann et al., 2013</a>)</cite>. Both of these OTS schemes are hash-based stateful signatures and need secure state management. We consider that OTS consists of: (i) <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OTS.Gen(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OTS.Gen(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> which takes the security parameter <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> as input and outputs a private and public key pair. (ii) <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OTS.Sign_{Sk}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OTS.Sign_{Sk}(m)</annotation></semantics></math>, which takes a message <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and the OTS private key <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Sk" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Sk</annotation></semantics></math> and outputs a signature <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. (iii) <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="OTS.Verify_{Pk}(&lt;m&gt;,\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OTS.Verify_{Pk}(&lt;m&gt;,\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math> which takes a message <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, an OTS signature <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and a public key <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Pk" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Pk</annotation></semantics></math> and outputs 1 if the signature is valid, and 0 otherwise.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The user <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> determines the maximum message budget <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{tot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{tot}</annotation></semantics></math> for
<math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ICP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ICP}</annotation></semantics></math>, and creates <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> OTS key pairs such that <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{tot}=n\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{tot}=n\times m</annotation></semantics></math>. It constructs a Merkle tree over the OTS public keys and signs
the Merkle root along with the hash chain length:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{U^{*}}}(\mathit{Mroot},\;n)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗀𝗇</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑀𝑟𝑜𝑜𝑡</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{U^{*}}}(\mathit{Mroot},\;n).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It then sends the Merkle tree and signature to the master agent <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and delegates the OTS private keys to <math id="A3.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving a task from <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, agent <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> processes it and
obtains the workflow, which identifies the first agent <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[1,t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[1,t]</annotation></semantics></math>, to contact. It derives a personalized hash chain of length <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>
using the seed:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A^{*}_{I}},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}},\;\mathit{addr})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖱𝖥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A^{*}_{I}},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}},\;\mathit{addr})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and extends it as <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}=H(s_{j-1},\,j,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}=H(s_{j-1},\,j,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.I3.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>. It then signs the chain root
using one of the delegated OTS private keys:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{A^{*}_{I}}_{\mathit{OTS}}=\mathsf{OTS.Sign}_{\mathit{OTS.sk}}(s_{n})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝑂𝑇𝑆</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖮𝖳𝖲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗀𝗇</mi><mrow><mi>𝑂𝑇𝑆</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>𝑠𝑘</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{A^{*}_{I}}_{\mathit{OTS}}=\mathsf{OTS.Sign}_{\mathit{OTS.sk}}(s_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Secure state management is assumed to prevent reuse of any OTS key.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> initiates an A-session with <math id="A3.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, it sends the
following to <math id="A3.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ul id="A3.I3.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the Merkle root <math id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Mroot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑀𝑟𝑜𝑜𝑡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Mroot}</annotation></semantics></math> and user signature
<math id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the OTS public key used to sign <math id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, together with a Merkle
proof that this key is included in the tree signed by <math id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the OTS signature <math id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{A^{*}_{I}}_{\mathit{OTS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝑂𝑇𝑆</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{A^{*}_{I}}_{\mathit{OTS}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the chain openings <math id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where
<math id="A3.I3.i3.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}=H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}=H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Agent <math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies the following:</p>
<ul id="A3.I3.i4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the user’s signature: <math id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{U^{*}}}(\langle\mathit{Mroot},\,n\rangle,\,\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵𝖾𝗋𝗂𝖿𝗒</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝑀𝑟𝑜𝑜𝑡</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{U^{*}}}(\langle\mathit{Mroot},\,n\rangle,\,\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}})=1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the OTS signature: <math id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{OTS.Verify}_{\mathit{OTS.pk}}(\langle s_{n}\rangle,\,\sigma^{A^{*}_{I}}_{\mathit{OTS}})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖮𝖳𝖲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵𝖾𝗋𝗂𝖿𝗒</mi><mrow><mi>𝑂𝑇𝑆</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>𝑝𝑘</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝑂𝑇𝑆</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{OTS.Verify}_{\mathit{OTS.pk}}(\langle s_{n}\rangle,\,\sigma^{A^{*}_{I}}_{\mathit{OTS}})=1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the Merkle proof is valid,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the hash step: <math id="A3.I3.i4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}=H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}=H(s_{n-1},\,n,\,\mathit{sid},\,\mathit{aid}_{A_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.I3.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If all checks pass, <math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is assured that <math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> has authorized a hash
chain of length <math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> for agent <math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to fulfill the task. Agent <math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> then
initializes a counter <math id="A3.I3.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{ctr}_{\mathit{ICP}}=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑐𝑡𝑟</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{ctr}_{\mathit{ICP}}=n</annotation></semantics></math> and decrements it
by one.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">In the next rounds, the initiator agent just sends a hash token from the chain <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the responding agent <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies that <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j}=H(s_{j-1},j,sid,aid_{A_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j}=H(s_{j-1},j,sid,aid_{A_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and then decreases the counter <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ctr_{ICP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ctr_{ICP}</annotation></semantics></math>. When the counter <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ctr_{ICP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ctr_{ICP}</annotation></semantics></math> reaches 0 it checks that <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}=PRF(sid,aid_{A^{*}_{I}},aid_{A_{i}},addr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}=PRF(sid,aid_{A^{*}_{I}},aid_{A_{i}},addr)</annotation></semantics></math>. If the agent wants to continue interactions and use more hash chains, it can increment <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="addr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">addr</annotation></semantics></math> by 1, and repeat the last two steps mentioned above to start a new personalized hash chain.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ICP in the two-agent case.</span> In the two-agent scenario, ICP becomes similar to RCP, and we deal with it in the same way using the same message count tokens used in RCP description. Therefore, the agent creates the hash chains of the length determined by the policy, and the user signs the hash terminal value. Then, agent sends the message count token and the signature to the responding agent.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>User-Agent Interaction for Multi-agent Setting</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assume the communication between the user and the master agent is local. In the agent registration subprotocol, the user has determined the ICP and RCP policies for all agents. For ICP which defines the maximum interaction budget for total requests, user has determined <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{tot}=n^{\prime}\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{tot}=n^{\prime}\times m</annotation></semantics></math>, and has shared <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with the master agent. When the user allocates the task to the master agent <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following subprotocol is run:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Giving the task to the agent.</span> The user <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> determines
the task <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{tsk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑡𝑠𝑘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{tsk}</annotation></semantics></math> and sends it to the master agent <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Executing the task and obtaining the workflow.</span> The master
agent <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> processes the task and derives the workflow, which specifies
the list of agents <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{1},\ldots,A_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{1},\ldots,A_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> that <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> must contact to
fulfill the task.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Creating the hash chain tokens.</span> Agent <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> generates
<math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> personalized hash chains. For each chain <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[0,m-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[0,m-1]</annotation></semantics></math>, the seed
is derived as:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{i}_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A^{*}_{I}},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}},\;\mathit{addr})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖱𝖥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑎𝑑𝑑𝑟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{i}_{0}=\mathsf{PRF}(\mathit{sid},\;\mathit{aid}_{A^{*}_{I}},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}},\;\mathit{addr}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the chain is extended as:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rho^{i}_{k}=H(\rho^{i}_{k-1},\;k,\;\mathit{sid}_{j},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}}),\qquad k=1,\ldots,n^{\prime}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑑</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{i}_{k}=H(\rho^{i}_{k-1},\;k,\;\mathit{sid}_{j},\;\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}}),\qquad k=1,\ldots,n^{\prime},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑎𝑖𝑑</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{aid}_{A_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity of the agent assigned to chain
<math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> according to the workflow, such that each agent receives at least one
chain. Agent <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> then sends the hash roots
<math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\rho^{i}_{n^{\prime}}\}_{i\in[0,m-1],\,j\in[1,t]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\rho^{i}_{n^{\prime}}\}_{i\in[0,m-1],\,j\in[1,t]}</annotation></semantics></math> to the user <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Creating the Merkle tree and signing the root.</span> The user
<math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> constructs a Merkle tree over the hash roots
<math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\rho^{i}_{n^{\prime}}\}_{i\in[0,m-1],\,j\in[1,t]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\rho^{i}_{n^{\prime}}\}_{i\in[0,m-1],\,j\in[1,t]}</annotation></semantics></math> received from <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>,
obtaining the root <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Mroot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑀𝑟𝑜𝑜𝑡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Mroot}</annotation></semantics></math>. The user signs the root as:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{U^{*}}}(\mathit{Mroot},\;n^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗀𝗇</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑀𝑟𝑜𝑜𝑡</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}=\mathsf{HS.Sign}_{sk_{U^{*}}}(\mathit{Mroot},\;n^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The user then sends the Merkle tree and signature
<math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5)</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Verifying the signature.</span> Agent <math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> verifies
<math id="A4.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}</annotation></semantics></math> by checking:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{U^{*}}}\!\left(\langle\,\mathit{Mroot},\;n^{\prime}\,\rangle,\;\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}\right)=1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖧𝖲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵𝖾𝗋𝗂𝖿𝗒</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝑀𝑟𝑜𝑜𝑡</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>𝐼𝐶𝑃</mi><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{HS.Verify}_{pk_{U^{*}}}\!\left(\langle\,\mathit{Mroot},\;n^{\prime}\,\rangle,\;\sigma^{U^{*}}_{\mathit{ICP}}\right)=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.i5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and stores the Merkle tree upon success.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the dynamic workflow, note that the Merkle tree is constructed over the OTS keys and the protocol have been described in Section <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Cryptographic Enforcement of Policies ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>UC Model and Ideal Functionalities</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below we give an overview of the UC approach and the description of each ideal functionality that is needed in our analysis.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1. </span>UC Approach</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the UC approach, the desired behavior of a system is specified by an
<em id="A5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ideal functionality</em> <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, which describes the working of the system in ideal world. Security of a protocol <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by comparing
the real-world execution of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> in the presence of an adversary <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>
with the ideal-world execution of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the adversary’s behavior
is emulated by a <em id="A5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">simulator</em> <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Protocol participants, <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{2}\cdots P_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{2}\cdots P_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, are modeled by polynomially-bounded Interactive Turing Machines (ITM).
A special ITM <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, called the <em id="A5.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">environment</em>, models the influence
of the surrounding protocol execution on <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. The environment provides inputs
to the participants, receives the outputs of honest parties, has access to the corrupted parties through <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, and may interact arbitrarily with
<math id="A5.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The protocol <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is UC-secure </span>if no environment <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> can distinguish between the real-world and ideal-world execution of the protocol.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2. </span>Global Clock Ideal Functionality <math id="A5.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow the clock functionality of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Canetti et al., 2017</a>)</cite> that provides a universal reference (physical) clock. When it is queried it provides an abstract notion of the time represented by <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. The clock is monotonic and only the environment can increment it; also the simulator cannot forge this reference time.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F11" class="ltx_figure" aria-describedby="acmlabel11">
<p id="A5.F11.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">
<span id="A5.F11.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A5.F11.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A5.F11.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Global clock ideal functionality <math id="A5.F11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math>
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.F11.3.1.2" class="ltx_p">maintains an integer <math id="A5.F11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to the reference time. When created, it initializes to <math id="A5.F11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
<span id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving message <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ClockUpdate,sid)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ClockUpdate,sid)</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, update <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\tau+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\tau+1</annotation></semantics></math> and send <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ClockUpdate,sid,ok)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ClockUpdate,sid,ok)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>. Ignore any clock update message sent by an other party.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ClockRead,sid)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ClockRead,sid)</annotation></semantics></math> from any entity return <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(clock\text{-}read,\;sid,\;\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(clock\text{-}read,\;sid,\;\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> to the requester.</span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>. </span><span id="A5.F11.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Global clock ideal functionality <math id="A5.F11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Canetti et al., 2017</a>)</cite></span><span id="acmlabel11" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">To avoid warning.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3. </span>Secure Communication Session Ideal Functionality <math id="A5.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}</annotation></semantics></math> </h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This functionality captures the security requirements of the TLS channel and allows a secure communication between entities in a single protocol instance. TLS consists of two phases: handshake and message transmission. The handshake protocol aims at securely sharing uniformly distributed session keys, and the message transmission provides authenticated encryption of session messages. The following ideal functionality <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gajek et al., 2008</a>)</cite> consists of session establishment and message sending and captures the security requirements of the TLS session which are: (i) <span id="A5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Uni- and bi-directional authentication (non-transferrable authentication)</span>. In uni-directional authentication mode, this functionality allows the adversary to impersonate the initiator. However, the adversary cannot impersonate the initiator after the two parties start communicating with each other. (ii) <span id="A5.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Confidentiality of messages.</span> This property is captured since adversary can only see the message of corrupted parties, and only receives a leakage <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l(m)</annotation></semantics></math> for messages of honest parties. The leakage function in TLS includes the message length and the TLS error messages. (iii) <span id="A5.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Integrity.</span>
Adversary cannot change the honest parties’ messages (in practice these messages have a sequence number that comes from the application layer to prevent changing their order). Adversary can only send corrupted messages to corrupted parties of its choice. We consider that <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}</annotation></semantics></math> captures the security properties of the post quantum TLS channel (that uses post-quantum secure primitives) as well.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F12" class="ltx_figure" aria-describedby="acmlabel12">
<p id="A5.F12.3" class="ltx_p">

<span id="A5.F12.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A5.F12.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A5.F12.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Functionality <math id="A5.F12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{scs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{scs}</annotation></semantics></math></span>, proceeds as follows, when parameterized by a leakage function <math id="A5.F12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l:\{0,1\}^{*}\rightarrow\{0,1\}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l:\{0,1\}^{*}\rightarrow\{0,1\}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
<span id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_centering">
<span id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving an input <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(establish\text{-}session,sid,IDI)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(establish\text{-}session,sid,IDI)</annotation></semantics></math> from some party, where <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="IDI\in(\perp,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⟂</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">IDI\in(\perp,I)</annotation></semantics></math>, record <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="IDI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">IDI</annotation></semantics></math> as initiator, and send the message to the adversary. Upon receiving input <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(establishsession,sid,R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(establishsession,sid,R)</annotation></semantics></math> from some party, record <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> as responder, and forward the message to the adversary.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving a value <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(impersonate,sid)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(impersonate,sid)</annotation></semantics></math> from the adversary, do: If <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(IDI=\perp)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(IDI=\perp)</annotation></semantics></math>, check that no ready entry exists, and record the adversary as initiator. Else ignore the message.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving a value <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(send,sid,m,P^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(send,sid,m,P^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> from party <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, which is either initiator or responder, check that a record <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sid,P,P^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sid,P,P^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> exists, record ready (if there is no such entry) and send <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sent,sid,l(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sent,sid,l(m))</annotation></semantics></math> to the adversary and a private delayed value <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(receive,sid,m,P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(receive,sid,m,P)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Else ignore the message. If the sender is corrupted, then disclose <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> to the adversary. Next, if the adversary provides <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and no output has been written to the receiver, then send <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(send,sid,\hat{m},\hat{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(send,sid,\hat{m},\hat{P})</annotation></semantics></math> to the receiver unless <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is an identity of an uncorrupted party.</span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>. </span><span id="A5.F12.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The secure communication session ideal functionality, <math id="A5.F12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="acmlabel12" class="ltx_nodisplay ltx_acm_description">To avoid warning.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4. </span>Global Random Oracle Ideal Functionality <math id="A5.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The random oracle functionality <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Camenisch et al., 2018</a>)</cite> has a <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="query" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">query</annotation></semantics></math> interface, and responds to all queries with uniformly random sampled values <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leftarrow\{0,\;1\}^{l(\kappa)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leftarrow\{0,\;1\}^{l(\kappa)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and outputs the same value for the same query.
<math id="A5.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> allows the adversary to program the random oracle to its desired values. At the same time, to prevent the adversary from programming collisions, it allows the parties to check whether a query has been programmed or not and drop that value if so. Additionally, the adversary can observe all the adversarial queries made from a wrong session <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{sid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{sid}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F13" class="ltx_figure" aria-describedby="acmlabel13">
<p id="A5.F13.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">
<span id="A5.F13.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:331.2pt;">
<span id="A5.F13.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A5.F13.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Functionality <math id="A5.F13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A5.F13.3.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F13.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Shared functionality </span><math id="A5.F13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> is globally available to all participants. It takes as input queries </span><math id="A5.F13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\{0,1\}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\{0,1\}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> and outputs values </span><math id="A5.F13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\{0,1\}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\{0,1\}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">. Internally, it stores initially empty sets </span><math id="A5.F13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, </span><math id="A5.F13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, and a set </span><math id="A5.F13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{sid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{sid}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.2.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> for all sessions </span><math id="A5.F13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sid" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sid</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.2.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
<span id="A5.F13.3.1.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A5.F13.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Query
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A5.F13.3.1.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">– Upon receiving </span><math id="A5.F13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(query,\;sid,\;q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(query,\;sid,\;q)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> from a party of session </span><math id="A5.F13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sid^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sid^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> proceed as follows:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I3" class="ltx_itemize ltx_align_left">
<span id="A5.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">If </span><math id="A5.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sid,\;q,\;r)\in L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sid,\;q,\;r)\in L</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> respond with </span><math id="A5.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(query,\;q,\;r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(query,\;q,\;r)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">If </span><math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sid,\;q,\;r)\notin L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∉</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sid,\;q,\;r)\notin L</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, samples </span><math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\{0,1\}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\{0,1\}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, store </span><math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sid,\;q,\;r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sid,\;q,\;r)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> in </span><math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> and respond with </span><math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(query,\;q,\;r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">y</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(query,\;q,\;r)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">If the query is made from a wrong session </span><math id="A5.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sid\neq sid^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≠</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sid\neq sid^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, store </span><math id="A5.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,\;r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,\;r)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> in </span><math id="A5.I3.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{sid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{sid}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.F13.3.1.4" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A5.F13.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Program
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A5.F13.3.1.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">– Upon receiving message </span><math id="A5.F13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(program,\;sid,\;q,\;r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(program,\;sid,\;q,\;r)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> by the adversary, check if </span><math id="A5.F13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sid,\;q,\;r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sid,\;q,\;r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> is defined in </span><math id="A5.F13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">. If this is the case, abort. Otherwise, if </span><math id="A5.F13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\{0,1\}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\{0,1\}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> store </span><math id="A5.F13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sid,\;q,\;r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sid,\;q,\;r)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> in </span><math id="A5.F13.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.4.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> and </span><math id="A5.F13.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sid,\;q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sid,\;q)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.4.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> in </span><math id="A5.F13.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.4.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
<span id="A5.F13.3.1.5" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A5.F13.3.1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">– Upon receiving </span><math id="A5.F13.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(isPrgrmd,\;q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(isPrgrmd,\;q)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.5.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> from a party of session </span><math id="A5.F13.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sid" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sid</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, check if </span><math id="A5.F13.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sid,\;q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sid,\;q)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> in </span><math id="A5.F13.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">. If this is the case respond with </span><math id="A5.F13.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(isPrgmd,\;1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em"> 1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(isPrgmd,\;1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.5.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
<span id="A5.F13.3.1.6" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A5.F13.3.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Observe
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A5.F13.3.1.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">– Upon receiving message </span><math id="A5.F13.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(observe)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(observe)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> from the adversary </span><math id="A5.F13.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> of session id </span><math id="A5.F13.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sid" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sid</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> respond with </span><math id="A5.F13.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(observe,\;L_{sid})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(observe,\;L_{sid})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F13.3.1.6.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F13.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 13</span>. </span><span id="A5.F13.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Global restricted programmable and observable random oracle functionality <math id="A5.F13.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Camenisch et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, provides three interfaces <span id="A5.F13.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Query</span>, <span id="A5.F13.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Program</span>, and <span id="A5.F13.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Observe</span> to participants.
</span><span id="acmlabel13" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">To avoid warning.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.5. </span>Certification Authority Ideal Functionality <math id="A5.SS5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Canetti, 2004</a>)</cite> for the ideal functionality of <math id="A5.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Figure <a href="#A5.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ E.5. Certification Authority Ideal Functionality ℱ_𝖢𝖠 ‣ Appendix E UC Model and Ideal Functionalities ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>). This ideal functionality is bound to a single identity via sid. <math id="A5.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math> accepts only the first registered message and does not allow for modification or revocation. <math id="A5.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math> does not perform any computation on the received message and only acts as the public bulletin board.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F14" class="ltx_figure" aria-describedby="acmlabel14">
<p id="A5.F14.3" class="ltx_p">

<span id="A5.F14.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A5.F14.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A5.F14.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Functionality <math id="A5.F14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{CA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{CA}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A5.I4" class="ltx_itemize ltx_centering">
<span id="A5.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving the first message <math id="A5.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Register,sid,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Register,sid,v)</annotation></semantics></math> from party <math id="A5.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, send <math id="A5.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Registered,sid,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Registered,sid,v)</annotation></semantics></math> to the adversary; upon receiving <math id="A5.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ok" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ok</annotation></semantics></math> from the adversary, and if <math id="A5.I4.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sid=P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sid=P</annotation></semantics></math>, and this is the first request from <math id="A5.I4.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>, then record the pair <math id="A5.I4.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(P,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(P,v)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving a message <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Retrieve,sid)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Retrieve,sid)</annotation></semantics></math> from party <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, send <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Retrieve,sid,P^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Retrieve,sid,P^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> to the adversary, and wait for an <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ok" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ok</annotation></semantics></math> from the adversary. Then, if there is a recorded pair <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sid,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sid,v)</annotation></semantics></math> output <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Retrieve,sid,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Retrieve,sid,v)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Else, output <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(Retrieve,sid,\perp)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⟂</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Retrieve,sid,\perp)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 14</span>. </span><span id="A5.F14.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The certification authority ideal functionality, <math id="A5.F14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="acmlabel14" class="ltx_nodisplay ltx_acm_description">To avoid warning.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.6. </span>Secure Registration Ideal Functionality <math id="A5.SS6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Reg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Reg}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A5.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Reg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Reg}</annotation></semantics></math> to capture the secure registration of the users and the agents (see Figure <a href="#A5.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ E.6. Secure Registration Ideal Functionality 𝐹_{𝑅⁢𝑒⁢𝑔} ‣ Appendix E UC Model and Ideal Functionalities ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>). The user <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> can choose a specific provider <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TA</annotation></semantics></math> to register with and choose a password <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Pwd" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Pwd</annotation></semantics></math> that will be stored with its identity (capturing that the user holds a certified public key) and will be used for authentication when registering the agents.
It also allows a user who has registered with an authorized <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TA</annotation></semantics></math> to register its agent <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> with attribute <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="attr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">attr</annotation></semantics></math>. The agent information consisting of the user identity, the agent identity, and the agent attribute are stored in the list of registered agents <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{AReg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{AReg}</annotation></semantics></math>. The adversary learns about the identity of the registered agents (we assume they are publicly known). <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Reg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Reg}</annotation></semantics></math> also allows the user <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>
to add or update a contact policy for its agent. The contact policy
<math id="A5.SS6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CP_{A}=\{[\mathsf{Send}/\mathsf{Receive},A_{i},\mathsf{Budget}_{i}]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖲𝖾𝗇𝖽</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖼𝖾𝗂𝗏𝖾</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝖡𝗎𝖽𝗀𝖾𝗍</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CP_{A}=\{[\mathsf{Send}/\mathsf{Receive},A_{i},\mathsf{Budget}_{i}]\}</annotation></semantics></math> specifies
which agents <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> may send requests to, or receive requests from, <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, together
with the corresponding contact budget <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Budget}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖡𝗎𝖽𝗀𝖾𝗍</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Budget}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The adversary is only informed about the call but nothing beyond that, which captures the fact that the communication is over PQ-TLS channel and the adversary can only learn if the user <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> has contacted the provider without knowing for which of the agents it has contacted nor for what purpose, that is, adding a policy or updating a policy.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F15" class="ltx_figure" aria-describedby="acmlabel15">
<p id="A5.F15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.F15.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:3.0pt;">

<span id="A5.F15.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A5.F15.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A5.F15.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Secure registration ideal functionality <math id="A5.F15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Reg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Reg}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="A5.F15.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, has access to the list of registered providers </span><math id="A5.F15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{TA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{TA}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F15.3.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, and holds a list </span><math id="A5.F15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{UReg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{UReg}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F15.3.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and </span><math id="A5.F15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{AReg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{AReg}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.F15.3.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> containing the identity of the registered user and the registered agents respectively.</span></span>
<span id="A5.I5" class="ltx_itemize ltx_centering">
<span id="A5.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Upon receiving an input </span><math id="A5.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(RegisterUser,sid,U,Pwd,TA)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(RegisterUser,sid,U,Pwd,TA)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> from some party </span><math id="A5.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, check </span><math id="A5.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TA\in L_{TA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TA\in L_{TA}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, also check </span><math id="A5.I5.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> has not been registered before, send </span><math id="A5.I5.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(RegisterUser,sid,TA,U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(RegisterUser,sid,TA,U)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> to the adversary; upon receiving ok from the adversary store </span><math id="A5.I5.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(TA,U,Pwd)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(TA,U,Pwd)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> in </span><math id="A5.I5.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{UReg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{UReg}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">.</span></span