<span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Upon receiving </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Task,sid,tsk,A^{*}_{I},attr^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Task,sid,tsk,A^{*}_{I},attr^{*})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> from user </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, where </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tsk" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tsk</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> is the given task from user </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> to </span><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">orchestrator</span><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> agent </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> with attribute </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="attr^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">attr^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, then store </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sid,tsk,U^{*},A^{*}_{I},attr^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">U</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sid,tsk,U^{*},A^{*}_{I},attr^{*})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> (if </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tsk=\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em">⟂</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tsk=\perp</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> aborts).
Next, run </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(A_{i},attr_{i},req^{1}_{i})\leftarrow ExeRes(A^{*}_{I},tsk,\perp)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">E</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⟂</mo><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{i},attr_{i},req^{1}_{i})\leftarrow ExeRes(A^{*}_{I},tsk,\perp)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> where </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ExeRes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ExeRes</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> runs the code of </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> on the given task </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tsk" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tsk</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and outputs the first request </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="req^{1}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">req^{1}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and the identity </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{i},attr_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{i},attr_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> of the first agent that needs to be contacted. Then, retrieve and parse </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="APolicy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">APolicy</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> from </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{APo}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{APo}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> for </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.20" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, that is, </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[(A^{*}_{I},\perp),Q_{tot},\Delta_{tot}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⟂</mo><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[(A^{*}_{I},\perp),Q_{tot},\Delta_{tot}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.21" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">. Next compute </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{exp}=\tau+\Delta_{tot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">τ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{exp}=\tau+\Delta_{tot}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.22" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">. Also, start a counter </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ctr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ctr</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.p1.1.23" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> for interaction limit. It then simulates the task execution internally as below:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I10.i2.I1" class="ltx_description">
<span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–Request handling:: </span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_item">
<span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">upon receiving </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Request,sid,A_{i},req^{k}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Request,sid,A_{i},req^{k}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> from </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> with attribute </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="att^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">att^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, check </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(AuthorizationAllowed,\cdot,A^{*}_{I},attr^{*},A_{i},attr_{i})\in L_{Auth}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(AuthorizationAllowed,\cdot,A^{*}_{I},attr^{*},A_{i},attr_{i})\in L_{Auth}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">; if so then
send </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ClockRead,sid)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ClockRead,sid)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> to </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">𝒢</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and get the time </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">. If this is the first time a request is received from </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, retrieve and parse </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="APolicy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">APolicy</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> from </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{APo}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{APo}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> for agent </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and retrieve </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[(A^{*}_{I},A_{i}),Q_{*,i},\Delta_{*,i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[(A^{*}_{I},A_{i}),Q_{*,i},\Delta_{*,i}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">. Then, check </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{*,i}&lt;\Delta_{tot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{*,i}&lt;\Delta_{tot}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and compute </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}_{exp}=\tau+\Delta_{*,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">τ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}_{exp}=\tau+\Delta_{*,i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">. Check that </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}_{exp}&lt;T_{exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}_{exp}&lt;T_{exp}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and store </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\prime}_{exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\prime}_{exp}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">. Else, abort. Also, start a counter </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ctr_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ctr_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> for interaction limit and increment both </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ctr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ctr</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ctr_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ctr_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.20" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">.
Else, if this is not the first message, check whether </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ctr_{i}\leq Q_{*,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">≤</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ctr_{i}\leq Q_{*,i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.21" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&lt;T^{\prime}_{exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">τ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&lt;T^{\prime}_{exp}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.22" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, and then increment </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ctr_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ctr_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.23" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> by one.
If the checks do not pass, abort and inform the adversary. Otherwise, run </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="res^{k}_{i}\leftarrow ExeReq(A_{i},tsk,req^{k}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">res^{k}_{i}\leftarrow ExeReq(A_{i},tsk,req^{k}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.24" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, and send </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Response,sid,A_{i},\ell(res^{k}_{i},Q_{*,i},\Delta_{*,i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Response,sid,A_{i},\ell(res^{k}_{i},Q_{*,i},\Delta_{*,i}))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.25" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> to the adversary.
Upon receiving abort from the adversary abort and output the identity of the corrupted agent, else proceed to </span><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.26" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">response handling</span><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.27" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–Response handling:: </span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_item">
<span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">upon receiving </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Response,sid,A^{*}_{I},res^{k}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Response,sid,A^{*}_{I},res^{k}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> from </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> with attribute </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="attr_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">attr_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, check whether </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ctr\leq Q_{tot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">≤</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ctr\leq Q_{tot}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, and increment </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ctr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ctr</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> by one; Then, check </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\leq T_{exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">τ</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">≤</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\leq T_{exp}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">. If the checks do not pass, abort and inform the adversary. Otherwise, run </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{j},attr_{j},req^{k+1}_{j},result)\leftarrow ExeRes(A^{*}_{I},tsk,res^{k}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{j},attr_{j},req^{k+1}_{j},result)\leftarrow ExeRes(A^{*}_{I},tsk,res^{k}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">. If </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j}=\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.800em">⟂</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j}=\perp</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, then output </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="result" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">result</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> and terminate. Else, send </span><math id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Request,sid,A_{j},\ell(req^{k+1}_{j},Q_{tot},\Delta_{tot}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Request,sid,A_{j},\ell(req^{k+1}_{j},Q_{tot},\Delta_{tot}))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> to adversary. Upon receiving abort from the adversary abort and output the identity of the corrupted agent, else proceed to </span><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">response handling</span><span id="A5.I10.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span><span id="A5.F19.3.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F19.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 19</span>. </span><span id="A5.F19.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The secure multi-agent composite session (C-session) ideal functionality, <math id="A5.F19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}</annotation></semantics></math> with dynamic workflow</span><span id="acmlabel19" class="ltx_nodisplay ltx_acm_description">To avoid warning.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Security Analysis</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we give the security analysis of MAGIQ in multiple steps as described in Figure <a href="#S5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 5.2. Modeling MAGIQ in the UC Approach ‣ 5. A Formalization of MAGIQ Properties ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1. </span>Main Theorem</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following theorem gives the security of MAGIQ:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Theorem F.1.</h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">MAGIQ  (Section <a href="#S4" title="4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) UC-realizes
<math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{A\text{-}\mathsf{auth}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the
<math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>-hybrid model.
The cryptographic building blocks of MAGIQ are (i) a digital signature scheme that is EUF-CMA, and (ii) hash function, HMAC and PRF that are modeled by global random oracles.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">(It is sufficient for the signature scheme that are used by all MAGIQ participants to be EUF-CMA in standard model).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof sketch.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We construct the protocol <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{MAGIQ}^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{MAGIQ}^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>-hybrid model and prove Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1. ‣ 5.3. Security Proof Sketch ‣ 5. A Formalization of MAGIQ Properties ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> through a sequence of lemmas, each capturing the security of one MAGIQ protocol. These protocols are executed sequentially: an agent may participate in an <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session or a <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session only after registration, and an initiating agent may start the session only after obtaining authorization from the <span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span>. The lemmas are stated below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hybrid world.</span> We consider a hybrid protocol <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}</annotation></semantics></math>. This means that we replace the PQ-TLS channel in the protocol with calls to <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}</annotation></semantics></math> Note that the protocol (specially the <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session) may run over multiple instances of <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, we assume parties have access to a certificate authority ideal functionality <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math> (that allows registering the identities by a trusted party and has been used in the security of TLS as well <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gajek et al., 2008</a>)</cite>), the global clock ideal functionality <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math> (that captures the reference clock) and the global random oracle ideal functionality <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> (that models the hash functions). We consider the adversary <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> to be static which means it corrupts the parties only before the protocol starts.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F20" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.06933v1/figures/A-sessionModel2.jpg" id="A6.F20.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/125;" width="286" height="125" alt="To avoid warning.">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F20.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 20</span>. </span><span id="A6.F20.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The <math id="A6.F20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session in the two-agent MAGIQ protocol</span><span id="acmlabel20" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">To avoid warning.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F21" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.06933v1/figures/C-ses-model2.jpg" id="A6.F21.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:191/151;" width="191" height="151" alt="To avoid warning.">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F21.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 21</span>. </span><span id="A6.F21.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The <math id="A6.F21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session in the multi-agent MAGIQ protocol</span><span id="acmlabel21" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">To avoid warning.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ideal world.</span> In the ideal world, we consider the ideal functionality <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> that captures the security of the protocol and interacts with a dummy user <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, and two agents <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a <span id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Provider</span> and uses the global clock ideal functionality <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the global random oracle functionality <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}}</annotation></semantics></math> as its subroutine (note that in our analysis, we only consider one protocol at a time, the entities that are involved in that protocol and the ideal functionality <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> that captures the security of that protocol.) Parties receive their inputs from the environment <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> and relay them to <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. When they receive their output from <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, they just pass it to <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>. We consider a simulator <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> that is the ideal world adversary which interacts with <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, and its goal is to simulate the protocol correctly such that <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot distinguish the ideal world protocol execution from the hybrid world. <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> has access to the code of the honest parties, some times denoted by <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Sim^{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Sim^{A}</annotation></semantics></math> for clarity, and can perform the computations internally. <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> can corrupt parties and in this case it gets oracle access to their codes.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2. </span>Security Analysis of the Registration Protocol</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we show that the user and agent registration protocol, described in Appendix <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>, UC realizes the registration ideal functionality <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma F.2.</h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The registration protocol of <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}</annotation></semantics></math> for the user and agent (described in Appendix <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>) UC realizes the registration ideal functionality <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}</annotation></semantics></math> against static adversaries.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> We analyze the security of the registration protocol considering that the user and provider are honest. Note that we have considered the provider to be semi-honest but we do not model the leakage against the provider since our goal is to only limit the information that provider can see from the agents communication, and we do not provide any cryptographic guarantee against a semi-honest provider. Below, we give the description of simulator <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simulating the provider.</span> <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> generates the identity and PQ-TLS key pairs <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sk_{TS},pk_{TA})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sk_{TS},pk_{TA})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sk^{tls}_{TA},pk^{tls}_{TA})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sk^{tls}_{TA},pk^{tls}_{TA})</annotation></semantics></math> for the provider, it also simulates <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math> by storing the identities of the provider <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(TA,pk_{TA})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(TA,pk_{TA})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(TA,pk^{tls}_{TA})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(TA,pk^{tls}_{TA})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> also simulates the provider’s certificates <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Cert^{tls}_{TA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Cert^{tls}_{TA}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Cert^{ID}_{TA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Cert^{ID}_{TA}</annotation></semantics></math> by signing its public keys using a generated key pair for the CA.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simulating the user registration.</span> Upon receiving <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(RegisterUser,sid,TA,U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(RegisterUser,sid,TA,U)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> generates the identity and PQ-TLS key pairs <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sk_{U},pk_{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sk_{U},pk_{U})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sk^{tls}_{U},pk^{tls}_{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sk^{tls}_{U},pk^{tls}_{U})</annotation></semantics></math> for the user, it also simulates <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math> by storing the identities of the user <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,pk_{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,pk_{U})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U,pk^{tls}_{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U,pk^{tls}_{U})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, it creates certificates for user’s public keys <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Cert^{tls}_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Cert^{tls}_{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Cert^{ID}_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Cert^{ID}_{U}</annotation></semantics></math> by signing the user’s public keys using a <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CA</annotation></semantics></math> private key (generated by <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math>). <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> also chooses a random value as password <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Pwd^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Pwd^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and stores it, sends ok to <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and sends a confirmation to the user.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simulating the agent registration.</span></p>
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(RegisterAgent,sid,U,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(RegisterAgent,sid,U,A)</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> generates PQ-TLS key pairs <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sk_{A},pk_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sk_{A},pk_{A})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sk^{tls}_{A},pk^{tls}_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sk^{tls}_{A},pk^{tls}_{A})</annotation></semantics></math> for the agent, and simulates <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math> by storing the identity of the agent <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,Pk^{tls}_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,Pk^{tls}_{A})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, it signs the identity public key of the agent using the user’s simulated keys, that is, <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U}_{ID}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mi>U</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U}_{ID}</annotation></semantics></math>. It also simulates the agent’s metadata, and signs the agent’s information <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U}_{A}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>U</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U}_{A}.</annotation></semantics></math> using the user’s key. Then, it sends ok to <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and sends the user the confirmation signature <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{TA}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{TA}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> which is generated on the agent’s info.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(AgentPolicy,sid,U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(AgentPolicy,sid,U)</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖱𝖾𝗀</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Reg}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> generates a contact policy <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CP_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CP_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> which is initially empty and stores it.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> fully simulates the user and agent protocol, since in this case, the user and provider are honest and <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> only sees the output of the honest parties. The output of user in this protocol is a confirmation message and a signature <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{TA}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{TA}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> that is simulated by <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> and it is indistinguishable from the real world values. We give the hybrid games for the in-distinguishability of the hybrid world from the ideal world in the full version of the paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3. </span>Security Analysis of Agent Discovery</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we show that the agent discovery protocol described in Section <a href="#S4" title="4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> UC realizes the <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session authorization ideal functionality <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma F.3.</h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The agent discovery protocol of <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}</annotation></semantics></math> (described in Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4. Agent-to-Agent Intercommunication ‣ 4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>) UC realizes the <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session authorization ideal functionality <math id="A6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}</annotation></semantics></math> against static adversaries.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> The agent discovery protocol is run between an agent and a provider. The provider is honest but the agent can be corrupted. We therefore consider two case: (i) the provider and agent are honest, and (ii) the provider is honest but the agent is corrupted. In the following, we give the description of the simulator <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> in this protocol considering that the registration protocols have been done as described in the previous section:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simulating PQ-TLS connection.</span> If both entities are honest, this step is not needed since environment does not have access to it. If the agent is corrupted, <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}</annotation></semantics></math> itself, and respond to the agent similar to <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simulating the agent’s authorization for <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session.</span> We consider the following cases:</p>
<ul id="A6.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case (i) Agent <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is honest.</span> Upon receiving <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Allowed,sid,A,attr,A^{\prime},attr^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Allowed,sid,A,attr,A^{\prime},attr^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates the information of agent <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of metadata, the endpoint descriptor, certificates, and user <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> signatures on the identity and information of <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> using random values, and generating private and public key pairs for <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, it retrieves the agent <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>’ identity and PQ-TLS public keys (note <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> can retrieve correct values since it simulates <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math> and we assume the registration protocol have been run beforehand) and generates <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{TA}_{ac}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{TA}_{ac}</annotation></semantics></math> on the <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> information and public keys of <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. It then returns the <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> information and <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{TA}_{ac}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{TA}_{ac}</annotation></semantics></math> to agent <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case (ii) Agent <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is corrupted.</span> In this case, <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> waits to receive <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(aid_{A},aid_{A^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(aid_{A},aid_{A^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and uses <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="aid_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">aid_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> (which incorporates <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Aid_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Aid_{U}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="aid_{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">aid_{U}</annotation></semantics></math> received from <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, rather than randomly generated values for user and agent identities. It retrieves the information of <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and if they have not registered yet, it aborts. The rest of the simulation is similar to above.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A6.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> fully simulates the agent discovery protocol; the reason is that <math id="A6.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> can simulate the view of the corrupted agent (by simulating <math id="A6.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math> internally) and the output of the agent (which is the agent information and provider’s signature) correctly using randomly generated values and the information it receives from the corrupted agent. We give the hybrid games for the in-distinguishability of the hybrid world from the ideal world in the full version of the paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.4. </span>Security Analysis of the <math id="A6.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session Protocol</h3>

<div id="A6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we show that the <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-sessionprotocol described in Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4. Agent-to-Agent Intercommunication ‣ 4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> (Figure <a href="#S4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 4.4.2. A-session protocol. ‣ 4.4. Agent-to-Agent Intercommunication ‣ 4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) between two agents <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> UC realizes the <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-sessionideal functionality <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma F.4.</h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session protocol (see Figure <a href="#A6.F20" title="Figure 20 ‣ Proof sketch. ‣ F.1. Main Theorem ‣ Appendix F Security Analysis ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) of <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}</annotation></semantics></math> (described in Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4. Agent-to-Agent Intercommunication ‣ 4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>) UC realizes the <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session ideal functionality <math id="A6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> against static adversaries.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> We consider three cases: (i) both <math id="A6.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> are honest, (ii) only <math id="A6.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> is corrupted, and (iii) only <math id="A6.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is corrupted. We give the simulations below:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case (i)</span> is straightforward since <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> only sees the output of honest agents. Assuming that the registration and agent discovery protocols have been simulated as described in previous subsections, and <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates the request and responses internally, the view of <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> is indistinguishable from the hybrid world. Note that <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> waits to receive <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Task,sid,A_{I},attr_{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Task,sid,A_{I},attr_{I})</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and replies <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Ok" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Ok</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, whenever <math id="A6.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts or terminates, it also aborts and terminates.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Below we only focus on the case where one of the agents is corrupted.
<math id="A6.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> receives messages from the ideal functionality <math id="A6.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the corrupted agent. Based on these messages, it has
to simulate the output of the honest parties and the full view of the corrupted parties.
Note that <math id="A6.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates <math id="A6.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}}</annotation></semantics></math> internally, and we assume it simulates the registration and agent discovery protocols as described in previous subsections.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case (ii): <math id="A6.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> is corrupted.</span> In this case, <math id="A6.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> has oracle access to the code of <math id="A6.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, and it has to simulate the view of <math id="A6.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and the output of the honest <math id="A6.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. For that, <math id="A6.SS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> translates the messages it receives from the corrupted <math id="A6.SS4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> for the ideal functionality <math id="A6.SS4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>and vice versa. It also simulates <math id="A6.SS4.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>’s output.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Handshake.</span> <math id="A6.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> waits until agent <math id="A6.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> initiates an <math id="A6.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session.</p>
<ul id="A6.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving the message <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{0},\sigma^{TA}_{ac},\sigma^{A_{I}}_{init},\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ICP})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{0},\sigma^{TA}_{ac},\sigma^{A_{I}}_{init},\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ICP})</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> parses <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}=(r_{1},info_{A_{I}},Q_{I,R},\Delta_{I,R},NextTk^{ICP}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}=(r_{1},info_{A_{I}},Q_{I,R},\Delta_{I,R},NextTk^{ICP}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> It sends <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ChangePolicy,sid,APolicy)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ChangePolicy,sid,APolicy)</annotation></semantics></math> from the user <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="APolicy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">APolicy</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[(A_{I},A_{R}),Q_{I,R},\Delta_{I,R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[(A_{I},A_{R}),Q_{I,R},\Delta_{I,R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖲𝖢𝖲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{SCS}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
It then verifies the validity of <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{TA}_{ac}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{TA}_{ac}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{A_{I}}_{init}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{A_{I}}_{init}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ICP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ICP}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="info_{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">info_{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math>, if they are valid it parses <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sid" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sid</annotation></semantics></math> and gets <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}(tsk)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}(tsk)</annotation></semantics></math>; Then, sends <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Observe" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Observe</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and retrieves <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tsk" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tsk</annotation></semantics></math>. It then sends <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Task,sid,tsk)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Task,sid,tsk)</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Else, it sends <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m24" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(Task,sid,\perp)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⟂</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Task,sid,\perp)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving the message <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Response,sid,A_{R},attr_{R},\ell=[Q^{*}_{R},\Delta^{*}_{R}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Response,sid,A_{R},attr_{R},\ell=[Q^{*}_{R},\Delta^{*}_{R}])</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>, store the message, and choose a symmetric key <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, compute <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{ses}=\mathcal{G}_{h}(r_{1},r_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{ses}=\mathcal{G}_{h}(r_{1},r_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Also compute the seed <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> through <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and compute the hash chain based on <span id="A6.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">task-msg</span> <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, let <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="NextTok^{RCP}_{0}=(\rho_{Q^{*}_{R}},\rho_{Q*_{R}-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>o</mi><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">NextTok^{RCP}_{0}=(\rho_{Q^{*}_{R}},\rho_{Q*_{R}-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, send <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}=r_{2},Q^{*}_{R},\Delta^{*}_{R},NextTok^{RCP}_{1},NextTok^{ICP}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}=r_{2},Q^{*}_{R},\Delta^{*}_{R},NextTok^{RCP}_{1},NextTok^{ICP}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, compute a tag <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tag_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tag_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{ses}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{ses}</annotation></semantics></math>, and send to <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Message transmission.</span></p>
<ul id="A6.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{i},tag_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{i},tag_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> parses <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}=(req_{i},NextTok^{ICP}_{i},NextTok^{RCP}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}=(req_{i},NextTok^{ICP}_{i},NextTok^{RCP}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, then it checks the validity of <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tag_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tag_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{ses}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{ses}</annotation></semantics></math> by querying <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also, program <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> by sending <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(program,sid,NextTok^{ICP}_{i},NextTok^{ICP}_{i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(program,sid,NextTok^{ICP}_{i},NextTok^{ICP}_{i-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts or the checks do not pass, upon receiving <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Request,sid,A_{I},attr_{I},\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Request,sid,A_{I},attr_{I},\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> abort. Else, send ok to <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, if <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>aborts, <math id="A6.I4.i1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> also aborts and terminates.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving a <math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Response,sid,A_{R},attr_{R},\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Response,sid,A_{R},attr_{R},\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates the response to the request <math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="req_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">req_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.To simulate the responder, <math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> executes the request internally using <math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ExeReq(A_{R},req_{i+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ExeReq(A_{R},req_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math> and gets the response <math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="res_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">res_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, it generates <math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i+1}=(res_{i+1},NextTok^{ICP}_{i+1},NextTok^{RCP}_{i+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i+1}=(res_{i+1},NextTok^{ICP}_{i+1},NextTok^{RCP}_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math>, and computes the tag using <math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{ses}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{ses}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="res_{i+1}\neq\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≠</mo><mo lspace="0em">⟂</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">res_{i+1}\neq\perp</annotation></semantics></math> send <math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ok" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ok</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.I4.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Else, aborts.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A6.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Note that if during the simulation <math id="A6.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}{scs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}{scs}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts, <math id="A6.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates another instance of <math id="A6.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also, whenever <math id="A6.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>aborts, <math id="A6.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts too.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case (iii): <math id="A6.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is corrupted.</span> In this case, <math id="A6.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> has oracle access to the code of <math id="A6.SS4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and it has to simulate the view of <math id="A6.SS4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and the output of the honest <math id="A6.SS4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. For that, <math id="A6.SS4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> translates the messages it receives from the corrupted <math id="A6.SS4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> for the ideal functionality <math id="A6.SS4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>and vice versa. It also simulates <math id="A6.SS4.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> internally.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Handshake.</span> <math id="A6.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> waits until agent <math id="A6.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> initiates establishing the session with <math id="A6.SS4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A6.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving the message <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Request,sid,A_{I},attr_{I},\ell=[Q^{*}_{I},\Delta^{*}_{I}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Request,sid,A_{I},attr_{I},\ell=[Q^{*}_{I},\Delta^{*}_{I}])</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates the establishment of a secure communication session <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}}</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.
It also parses <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sid" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sid</annotation></semantics></math> and extracts the task <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tsk" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tsk</annotation></semantics></math> by sending <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Observe" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Observe</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and stores <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tsk" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tsk</annotation></semantics></math>.
It then simulates <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{0},\sigma^{TA}_{ac},\sigma^{A_{I}}_{init},\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ICP})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{0},\sigma^{TA}_{ac},\sigma^{A_{I}}_{init},\sigma^{U_{I}}_{ICP})</annotation></semantics></math> and send it to <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}=(r_{1},info_{A_{I}},Q^{*}_{I},\Delta^{*}_{I},NextTk^{ICP}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}=(r_{1},info_{A_{I}},Q^{*}_{I},\Delta^{*}_{I},NextTk^{ICP}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen uniformly at random. Also, <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="info_{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">info_{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated based on the information <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> has obtained during the previous protocols such as registration and agent discovery, or generated randomly from the identical distribution as the real values. Next, send ok to <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts, <math id="A6.I5.i1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts and terminates.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving <math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{1},tag_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{1},tag_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> parses <math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}=(r_{2},Q_{R,I},\Delta_{R,I},NextTok^{RCP}_{1},NextTok^{ICP}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}=(r_{2},Q_{R,I},\Delta_{R,I},NextTok^{RCP}_{1},NextTok^{ICP}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, and verifies that <math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tag_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tag_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="NextTok^{ICP}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">NextTok^{ICP}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> are valid.
Also, parse <math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="NextTok^{RCP}_{1}=[s_{Q^{*}_{R}},s_{Q^{*}_{R}-1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">NextTok^{RCP}_{1}=[s_{Q^{*}_{R}},s_{Q^{*}_{R}-1}]</annotation></semantics></math> and program <math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> to output <math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{Q^{*}_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{Q^{*}_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> when queried by <math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{Q^{*}_{R}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{Q^{*}_{R}-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. If the checks pass and <math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> does not abort, send ok to <math id="A6.I5.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>, else aborts and terminates.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Message transmission.</span></p>
<ul id="A6.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving a <math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Request,sid,A_{I},attr_{I},\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Request,sid,A_{I},attr_{I},\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates the request <math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="req_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">req_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. To simulate the request, <math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> executes the response internally using <math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ExeRes(A_{R},tsk,req_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ExeRes(A_{R},tsk,req_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and gets the response <math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="res_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">res_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, it generates <math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}=(req_{i},NextTok^{ICP}_{i},NextTok^{RCP}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}=(req_{i},NextTok^{ICP}_{i},NextTok^{RCP}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, and computes the tag using <math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{ses}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{ses}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="req_{i}\neq\perp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≠</mo><mo lspace="0em">⟂</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">req_{i}\neq\perp</annotation></semantics></math>, it sends <math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ok" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ok</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.I6.i1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Else, aborts.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon receiving <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{i+1},tag_{i+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{i+1},tag_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> parses <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i+1}=(req_{i+1},NextTok^{ICP}_{i+1},NextTok^{RCP}_{i+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i+1}=(req_{i+1},NextTok^{ICP}_{i+1},NextTok^{RCP}_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math>, then it checks the validity of <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tag_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tag_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{ses}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{ses}</annotation></semantics></math> by querying <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also, program <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> by sending <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(program,sid,NextTok^{RCP}_{i+1},NextTok^{RCP}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(program,sid,NextTok^{RCP}_{i+1},NextTok^{RCP}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts or the checks do not pass, upon receiving <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Response,sid,A_{R},attr_{R},\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Response,sid,A_{R},attr_{R},\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> abort. Else, send ok to <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, if <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>aborts, <math id="A6.I6.i2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> also aborts and terminates.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A6.SS4.p10.2" class="ltx_p">Note that if during the simulation <math id="A6.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}{scs}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}{scs}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts, <math id="A6.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates another instance of <math id="A6.SS4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also, whenever <math id="A6.SS4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts, <math id="A6.SS4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts too.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p">The above simulation completely simulates the hybrid <math id="A6.SS4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session protocol since the simulator can extract the task, run the code of the honest agents on the task, and simulate the task messages correctly. Additionally, we assume that the signature scheme is EUF-CMA secure, so the corrupted agent cannot forge them, and the HMAC, hash function, and PRF are modeled by a random oracle, which means that their output are indistinguishable from random values. We give the hybrid games for the in-distinguishability of the hybrid world from the ideal world in the full version of the paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.5. </span>Security Analysis of the <math id="A6.SS5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session Protocol</h3>

<div id="A6.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we show that the <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-sessionprotocol described in Section <a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5. Multi-Agent Intercommunication ‣ 4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a> (Figure <a href="#S4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 4.4.2. A-session protocol. ‣ 4.4. Agent-to-Agent Intercommunication ‣ 4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) between the <span id="A6.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> agent <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and a set of <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> UC realizes the <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session ideal functionality <math id="A6.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma F.5.</h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session protocol (see Figure <a href="#A6.F21" title="Figure 21 ‣ Proof sketch. ‣ F.1. Main Theorem ‣ Appendix F Security Analysis ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) of <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖼𝗌</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝖠</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>𝖼𝗅𝗄</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{scs}},\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{CA}},\mathcal{G}_{\mathsf{clk}},\mathcal{G}_{h}}_{MAGIQ}</annotation></semantics></math> (described in Section <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4. Agent-to-Agent Intercommunication ‣ 4. MAGIQ Design ‣ MAGIQ: A Post-Quantum Multi-Agentic AI Governance System with Provable Security" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>) UC realizes the <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session ideal functionality <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖢𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Cses}}</annotation></semantics></math> against static adversaries assuming <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{Ases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{Ases}</annotation></semantics></math> UC realizes <math id="A6.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.5.1. </span>Proof.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider three cases: (i) all agents are honest, (ii) only <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is corrupted, and (iii) all <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are corrupted. We give the simulations below:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case (i).</span> This case is straightforward; when all agents are honest, <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates the ideal functionalities <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the output of honest agents correctly; it receives the task <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tsk" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tsk</annotation></semantics></math> from the dummy <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and it executes it internally and gets the subtasks that should be simulated in each <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> (see case (iii)).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case (ii).</span> When <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is corrupted, <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A^{*}_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A^{*}_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates the ideal functionalities <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the view of the corrupted <span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">orchestrator</span> (that is same as the simulated ideal functionalities) and output of honest agents correctly (see below):</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A6.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simulating each <math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> <math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A^{*}_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A^{*}_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> waits to receive 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(GetAuthorization,sid,A^{*}_{I},attr_{I},A_{i},attr_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(GetAuthorization,sid,A^{*}_{I},attr_{I},A_{i},attr_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}\in A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}\in A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and checks whether <math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are registered and their identities are in <math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CP_{A^{*}_{I}}\cap CP_{A_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CP_{A^{*}_{I}}\cap CP_{A_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If so, it retrieves the counter and checks wether they have enough <math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session budget. If so, it sends <math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Allowed,sid,A^{*}_{I},attr_{I},A_{i},attr_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Allowed,sid,A^{*}_{I},attr_{I},A_{i},attr_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and stores it in <math id="A6.I7.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{Auth}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{Auth}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simulating each <math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> For each <math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session  <math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A^{*}_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A^{*}_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> waits to receive <math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(AgentPolicy,sid,APolicy)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(AgentPolicy,sid,APolicy)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and stores <math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="APolicy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">APolicy</annotation></semantics></math>’s. Upon receiving <math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Task,sid,subtsk)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Task,sid,subtsk)</annotation></semantics></math> from the corrupted <math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, it internally runs the task execution on <math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="subtsk" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">subtsk</annotation></semantics></math>, and returns the result and terminates when the task execution completes. Also, note that whenever <math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts, <math id="A6.I7.i2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A^{*}_{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A^{*}_{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts and terminates.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case (iii).</span> When <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is corrupted, <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates the ideal functionalities <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the view of the corrupted <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (that is same as the simulated <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and output of <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{I}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{I}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> correctly (see below):</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A6.I8" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I8.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Receiving the policy and task from <math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> <math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> waits to receive <math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(AgentPolicy,sid,APolicy)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(AgentPolicy,sid,APolicy)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}\in A_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}\in A_{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and stores <math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="APolicy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">APolicy</annotation></semantics></math>’s. Upon receiving <math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Task,sid,tsk)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Task,sid,tsk)</annotation></semantics></math> from dummy <math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, it internally runs the task execution on <math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tsk" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tsk</annotation></semantics></math> and gets the schedule and the <math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="subtask" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">subtask</annotation></semantics></math>’s for each responding agent <math id="A6.I8.i1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I8.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simulating each <math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> <math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates the <math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖺𝗎𝗍𝗁</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{A\text{-}auth}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>; it checks whether <math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are registered and their identities are in <math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CP_{A^{*}_{I}}\cap CP_{A_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CP_{A^{*}_{I}}\cap CP_{A_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If so, it retrieves the counter and checks wether they have enough <math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-session budget. If the check passes, it sends <math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Allowed,sid,A^{*}_{I},attr_{I},A_{i},attr_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Allowed,sid,A^{*}_{I},attr_{I},A_{i},attr_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and stores it in <math id="A6.I8.i2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{Auth}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{Auth}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I8.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simulating each <math id="A6.I8.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> <math id="A6.I8.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> simulates <math id="A6.I8.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>𝖠𝗌𝖾𝗌</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\mathsf{Ases}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A6.I8.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="subtask" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">subtask</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.I8.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and returns the result and terminates when the task execution completes. Whenever <math id="A6.I8.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts, <math id="A6.I8.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝖲𝗂𝗆</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Sim}^{A_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> aborts and terminates.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The above simulation completely simulates the hybrid <math id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>-session protocol. We give the hybrid games for the in-distinguishability of the hybrid world from the ideal world in the full version of the paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS5.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Our analysis can be extended to the dynamic setting as well. We leave the complete proof for this setting to the full version of the paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
